/* 段落记忆 · 词层 1 · 子块 a：词头 → {tw:[关系词,关系类型], en, zh} */
window.APP_MERGE_NET(1,{"sub":"a","par":{"close":{"tw":[["closure",4],["end",2],["finish",2],["last",0],["complete",2],["draw",3],["plug",3],["open",1]],"en":"Last winter the town decided on the closure of the small library. Nobody wanted to see it close, but the money had run out. My neighbours signed a paper to ask for a new end date. After months of work we managed to complete the repairs ourselves and finish the roof before the cold came. On the last evening a reporter came to draw a picture of the empty hall. We pulled the plug of the old coffee machine and opened every window to let the dust out. It felt like an open door again.","zh":"去年冬天镇上决定关闭那间小图书馆。没有人想看着它关门，但经费已经用完了。邻居们签了一份请愿书，要求给一个新的截止日期。忙了几个月，我们自己修好了屋顶，赶在寒潮前把工程做完。最后一个晚上，一位记者来画下了空荡荡的大厅。我们拔掉了旧咖啡机的插头，把每扇窗都打开放灰尘出去。它又像一扇开着的门了。"},"climb":{"tw":[["steep",6],["raise",0],["move",2],["grow",2],["jump",3],["ride",3],["rise",2],["peak",6],["mount",0]],"en":"The path to the top is steep, and the last hour of it is a slow climb. We begin early, before the sun can raise the heat of the day. Step by step we move up and watch the farms below grow small. My brother likes to jump from rock to rock, while I prefer to ride the old cable car. Every spring more visitors rise with the first light, so we chose a quiet Tuesday instead. At the peak we mount a small flag on the stone and eat our bread in the wind.","zh":"上山顶的路很陡，最后一段更是一步一步地爬。我们很早就出发，趁太阳还没把热气升起来。一级一级往上走，看着下面的农庄变得越来越小。弟弟喜欢在石头间跳来跳去，我更愿意坐那趟旧缆车。每年春天都有更多游客跟着第一缕光上山，所以我们挑了安静的周二。到了山顶，我们在石头上竖了一面小旗，在风里啃面包。"},"decide":{"tw":[["decision",4],["settle",0],["determine",2],["judge",3],["decisive",4],["rule",3],["resolve",0],["agree",6]],"en":"Our class had to decide where to spend the last school trip. The teacher said the decision must come from us. First we tried to settle the money problem, because that would determine everything else. Two students wanted the sea and three wanted the hills. We asked our teacher to judge which plan was fair. In the end his most decisive answer was simple: ask more people. When the vote was over we had to rule out the far places and resolve one last question about the bus. Everyone agreed.","zh":"我们班得决定最后一次班级旅行去哪儿。老师说这个决定必须由我们自己来做。我们先想办法解决钱的问题，因为那会决定其他一切。两个同学想去海边，三个想去山里。我们请老师来评判哪个方案更公平。最后他给出的最果断的回答很简单：多问些人。投票结束后，我们只能排除太远的地方，再解决最后一个关于大巴的疑问。所有人都同意了。"},"difference":{"tw":[["different",4],["differ",4],["differentiate",4],["conflict",0],["balance",3],["gap",3],["remainder",0],["quality",2]],"en":"The two reports about the same meeting were very different. They differ on one point only: the cost. Nobody could explain the difference, and soon it turned into a small conflict. My job was to check the balance of the two lists and find the gap between them. The remainder was small, but the quality of the work was not the same at all. In the end we had to differentiate between what we measured and what we guessed. That one difference changed the whole decision, and afterwards the two teams never worked in the same room again.","zh":"同一场会议的两份报告很不一样。它们只在一个点上不同：成本。没人能解释这个差异，很快它就变成了一场小冲突。我的工作是核对两张清单是否平衡，找出它们之间的缺口。剩余的部分很小，但工作的质量完全不同。最后我们不得不区分哪些是我们实测的、哪些是猜的。正是这一个差异改变了整个决定，此后两支队伍再也没在同一间屋里共事过。"},"death":{"tw":[["die",4],["dead",6],["mortuary",4],["end",2],["grave",3],["birth",1],["destruction",0],["demise",0]],"en":"The death of the old king changed everything. Few people died in the war itself, but the destruction of the city killed the trade. In the mortuary they counted the bodies, and the dead were carried out at dawn. The grave of his father stood next to the new one. His birth had been a feast; his demise was a silence, and the end came quietly. For a whole year afterwards the shops stayed shut and nobody sang in the streets. The grave outside the wall is small, and no name was ever cut into the stone.","zh":"老国王的死改变了一切。战争本身没死几个人，但城市的毁灭扼杀了贸易。在停尸房里他们清点遗体，死者于黎明时被抬走。他父亲的墓就在新墓旁边。他的出生曾是一场盛宴，他的离世却是一片寂静，结局来得悄无声息。此后整整一年，店铺都关着，街上再没人唱歌。墙外那座墓很小，石头上始终没有刻名字。"},"admit":{"tw":[["admission",4],["accept",2],["allow",0],["permit",2],["deny",1],["acknowledge",6],["seat",3],["serve",2]],"en":"They will not admit more than fifty people. The admission desk is at the door: if they accept your ticket they allow you in, but the permit is only for one hour. They deny nothing and acknowledge every question, yet the room can serve only a few at a time. I could not find a single empty seat. Outside, a hundred people were still waiting in the rain, and nobody there looked angry. They simply waited while the rain fell on their coats and on the stone steps of the hall.","zh":"他们最多只放进五十个人。售票处在门口：如果他们收下你的票就允许你进去，但许可只限一小时。他们什么也不否认，对每个问题都有回应，可那间屋子一次只能招待几个人。我一个空座位都没找到。外面还有一百个人在雨里等着，而那边没有一个人显得生气。"},"arm":{"tw":[["armament",4],["disarm",1],["weapon",0],["sword",3],["bow",3],["instrument",2],["limb",2],["finger",6]],"en":"He hurt his left arm in the factory last month. The limb was not broken, but he cannot lift a heavy instrument any more, and his fingers are slow in the cold. In the old armament room next door they keep weapons behind glass: a bow, a sword, two long guns. The guard had to disarm a man there once, and the story is still told in the village. My brother works with one hand now and laughs about it. He says a man only needs one good arm to do the work of two.","zh":"他上个月在工厂里伤了左臂。那条胳膊没断，但他再也不能举起重工具了，天冷时手指也不灵活。隔壁那间旧军械室里，武器都用玻璃罩着：一张弓、一把剑、两杆长枪。守卫曾在那里缴过一个人的械，这事村里至今还在讲。我哥哥现在只用一只手干活，还拿这事开玩笑。他说一个人只要有一条好胳膊，就能干两条胳膊的活。"},"better":{"tw":[["bet",4],["best",0],["improve",0],["worse",1],["change",2],["build",3],["break",0],["help",3]],"en":"I made a bet with myself last spring. The best way to get better at this job, I decided, is to build one small habit and never break it. A change of hours will help; working later only makes things worse. I want to improve slowly, not quickly. My brother says I should rest more, and I am sure he is right, because he is a good worker and I am not. So far I have kept the bet for eleven weeks, and the work is easier than it was.","zh":"去年春天我和自己打了个赌。我认定，要把这活儿做得更好，最好的办法是养成一个小习惯并且不打破它。改一改作息会有帮助；干到更晚只会让情况更糟。我要慢慢提高，而不是求快。我哥哥说我该多休息，我确信他是对的，因为他是个好工人而我不是。到现在这个赌我守了十一周，活儿也比从前轻松了。"},"base":{"tw":[["basal",4],["bag",0],["bed",3],["bottom",2],["floor",0],["build",3],["control",2],["foot",0]],"en":"The base of the old tower is wider than the top. At the bottom there is a thick basal layer of stone, and below that only sand. We had to build a floor of wood over it so that nobody would fall through. Every bag of tools sits in the corner. From the control room you can see the whole valley, and it is a long way down to the foot of the hill. A bed of dry grass used to cover the stone, but the rain took it years ago.","zh":"那座古塔的基部比顶部宽。底部有一层很厚的基底石，再往下就只有沙子了。我们不得不在上面铺一层木地板，免得有人掉下去。每袋工具都堆在角落里。从控制室能看到整个山谷，往下到山脚还有很长一段路。从前有一层干草铺在石头上，但多年前就被雨水冲走了。"},"bet":{"tw":[["count",0],["pot",3],["trust",2],["raise",3],["gamble",2],["cash",6],["play",3],["better",4]],"en":"Do not bet on that horse. I do not trust the man who owns it, and I can count the times he has actually paid on one hand. The pot is small tonight, but he will raise it as soon as you sit down. My cousin likes to gamble and always plays with cash. You will feel better if you keep your money in your pocket. I learned that lesson in a single evening, and it was not a cheap one to learn. I still go to the track, but I only watch the horses and count my own money.","zh":"别赌那匹马。我不信任它的主人，他真正付过钱的次数我一只手就数得过来。今晚的赌池很小，可你一坐下他就会加注。我表弟喜欢赌，而且总是用现金玩。把钱留在口袋里你会好受些。我是在一个晚上学会这个教训的，而那学费并不便宜。我还会去马场，但只看马，只数自己的钱。"},"board":{"tw":[["boarder",4],["card",0],["catch",3],["enter",2],["commission",6],["room",0],["deal",3],["table",2]],"en":"The board meets at eight. Each member puts a card on the table, and the chairman reads out the name of every boarder in the house. We deal with one question at a time, and only one. A small commission was set up last year to check the accounts, and nobody has entered that room since March. I try to catch the chairman before the meeting, but he is never alone. Last week they sat for four hours and decided nothing at all. The card with my name is still on the table, and the room is still locked.","zh":"董事会八点开会。每位成员把一张卡片放在桌上，主席逐一念出屋里每位寄宿者的名字。我们一次只处理一个问题，而且只处理一个。去年成立了一个小委员会来查账，可自三月起没人进过那个房间。我想在会前逮住主席，可他从没落单过。上周他们坐了四个小时，什么也没定下来。桌上那张写着我名字的卡片还在，那个房间还锁着。"},"carry":{"tw":[["carriage",4],["bear",2],["deal",3],["act",2],["express",0],["fly",3],["bring",2],["hold",0]],"en":"I have to carry these boxes to the station. The carriage of the train leaves in an hour, and the porter will not bear more than two at a time. We deal with the heaviest first and then act quickly. If we are late they will not hold the train, and my sister will have to bring the rest tomorrow. The express never stops here. Nothing flies out of this town, so everything goes by rail. The porter says the same thing every winter, and every winter he turns out to be right.","zh":"我得把这些箱子搬到车站去。那趟火车的车厢一小时后开，搬运工一次不肯扛超过两箱。我们先处理最重的，然后动作要快。要是迟了他们不会等车，剩下的就得让我妹妹明天带来。快车从不停这里。这个镇上什么也飞不出去，所以一切都走铁路。"},"catch":{"tw":[["catchment",4],["see",0],["bag",3],["board",2],["stop",0],["fish",3],["throw",6],["view",0]],"en":"We could not catch a single fish all morning. The catchment above the dam is full of rain water and the fish are deep. I stood on the board and could not see a thing; my bag was still empty at noon. Then one careless throw of a stone by a boy on the far bank moved the whole shoal at once. From where I stood the view was lovely, but that does not stop me from wanting one fish. Next week I will try the other side, where the water is slower.","zh":"整个上午我们一条鱼也没抓到。水坝上游的集水区灌满了雨水，鱼都沉在深处。我站在木板上什么也看不见；到了中午我的袋子还是空的。后来一个男孩扔了块石头，整群鱼一下子全动了。从我站的地方看出去景色很美，可这并不能阻止我想要一条鱼。下周我要去另一边试试，那边水流更缓。"},"count":{"tw":[["counter",4],["bet",0],["total",3],["depend",0],["poll",3],["trust",2],["result",6],["look",0]],"en":"We count the votes twice. The counter at the front of the room is an old wooden table, and the total is written on the wall in chalk. You cannot depend on one count, and you cannot trust the first result either. At the last poll two hundred people came, and the look on his face said everything. I would bet the second count is the true one. Nobody argues after the second count; they simply pick up their coats and go home. The total goes on the wall in chalk, and the rain washes it off by morning.","zh":"我们把票点两遍。屋子前面那张计数器是一张旧木桌，总数用粉笔写在墙上。你不能只靠一次计数，也不能相信第一次的结果。上一次投票来了两百人，而他脸上的表情说明了一切。我敢打赌第二次计数才是真的。第二次计数之后没人再争，他们只是拿起外套回家。总数用粉笔写在墙上，到早上被雨冲掉。"},"die":{"tw":[["death",4],["break",0],["fall",3],["change",2],["pass",0],["crash",3],["feel",2],["fail",0]],"en":"Old engines do not die all at once. First a small part breaks, then the pressure falls, and the change is very slow. You can feel it in the steering wheel months before the end. If the pump fails, the car will crash into the wall at the next bend. The death of an engine is a long story, and most of it happens quietly. Mine passed away on a Tuesday, in front of my own house, with the key still in the door. I still feel for the brake when I hear that particular sound.","zh":"老发动机不会一下子死掉。先是某个小零件坏掉，接着压力下降，变化非常慢。在结局到来前几个月，你就能在方向盘上感觉到。如果水泵失灵，车会在下一个弯道撞上墙。一台发动机的死亡是个漫长的故事，而且大部分是悄无声息地发生的。我那台是在一个星期二咽气的，就在我自己家门口，钥匙还插在门上。每当听到那种特别的声音，我还是会去踩刹车。"},"doctor":{"tw":[["doctoral",4],["fix",0],["fill",3],["better",2],["nurse",6],["repair",0],["piece",3],["restore",0]],"en":"The doctor came at seven. He fixed my arm, filled a small cup with something bitter, and said I would feel better in a week. A nurse held the lamp; she said the same doctor had repaired her father's leg and restored it to full use. He showed me one small piece of bone in the palm of his hand. He is writing a doctoral paper about exactly this sort of injury. He told me I was lucky, and I did not argue with him. The nurse filled in the form, and he signed the bottom of the page.","zh":"医生七点来的。他给我接好了胳膊，倒了一小杯很苦的东西，说我一周后就会好些。一位护士举着灯；她说同一位医生修好过她父亲的腿，并让它完全恢复了功能。他摊开手掌给我看一小块骨头。他正在写一篇关于这类损伤的博士论文。他说我很幸运，我没有跟他争。护士填好表格，他在纸的下方签了名。"},"draw":{"tw":[["drawer",4],["force",0],["arrange",2],["match",6],["line",0],["catch",3],["win",6],["lot",0]],"en":"Let us draw for the first turn. In the drawer of the little table there are four cards; arrange them face down and each of us takes one. Catch your card before it falls on the floor. The match is won by the highest line, so look at it carefully. I never win anything by luck, and a lot of people at this table say the same. You can force the card if you want, but then there is no point in playing at all. I drew the lowest line, as usual, and the drawer was closed again.","zh":"咱们抽签决定先手吧。小桌的抽屉里有四张牌；把它们正面朝下摆好，每人拿一张。牌掉到地上之前接住它。比赛由点数最大的那一行获胜，所以要看仔细。我从来没靠运气赢过什么，这张桌上很多人也这么说。你想的话可以硬来，但那样玩起来就没意思了。我照例抽到了最小的一行，抽屉又合上了。"},"drive":{"tw":[["drift",4],["cause",0],["lift",3],["fight",2],["force",0],["pull",3],["hit",2],["push",0]],"en":"It is a long drive to the coast. The road begins to drift west after the bridge, and the wind can cause the car to lift on the open bends. My father would push the speed up and then pull it back again; he never liked to fight the wheel. One year a stone hit the glass and we ran the last ten miles with no window at all. I drive slowly now, and the force of the wind still surprises me every time. My son does not like the coast road, and I do not push him to drive it.","zh":"开车到海边要走很久。过了桥这条路就开始向西偏，在开阔的弯道上风能把车掀起来。我父亲会把速度推上去再收回来；他从不喜欢跟方向盘较劲。有一年一块石头打在玻璃上，我们最后十英里是没窗跑完的。我现在开得慢，而每次那股风力还是让我吃惊。我儿子不喜欢那条海边公路，我也不催他去开。"},"earth":{"tw":[["terrestrial",4],["ground",2],["floor",3],["concern",2],["space",6],["land",0],["forest",3],["hide",2],["world",0]],"en":"The earth here is red and thin. On the ground under the trees there is a soft floor of leaves, and the forest hides more than it shows. Scientists come to study the terrestrial plants; others look up at the space above the trees and forget the land under their feet. Their only concern is the rain, and the rain comes when it wants to. For me this small piece of earth is the whole world, and I do not want to leave it. The ground is soft in May and hard in August, and I know every metre of it.","zh":"这里的土又红又薄。树下的地面上铺着一层松软的落叶，森林藏起来的比露出来的多。科学家来研究陆生植物；另一些人抬头看树顶以上的太空，却忘了脚下的土地。他们唯一关心的是雨，而雨想来就来。对我来说这一小块土地就是整个世界，我不想离开它。五月的土地松软，八月就硬了，每一米我都熟。"},"edge":{"tw":[["edgy",4],["inch",0],["shoulder",3],["line",2],["march",0],["margin",3],["side",2],["border",3],["corner",6]],"en":"We walked along the edge of the field for an hour. The border with the next farm is only a line of small stones, and the margin of the wood lies on the far side. At the corner an old man was marching up and down with his shoulder against the wind. I moved an inch at a time, because the drop below was long. My friend felt edgy and would not look down once the whole way. We sat down at last, well back from the edge, and ate the bread we had brought.","zh":"我们沿着田边走了一个小时。与隔壁农场的分界只是一排小石头，树林的边缘在更远的一侧。拐角处有个老人顶着风来回踱步，肩膀迎着风口。我一次只挪一寸，因为下面的落差很大。我朋友一路上都很紧张，一次也没敢往下看。"},"book":{"tw":[["booking",4],["hold",0],["card",3],["register",2],["novel",6],["record",2],["ticket",3],["essay",6]],"en":"I read one book about the sea every winter. It is not a novel; it is the record of a man who worked on a boat for thirty years. He could not hold a pen at first, so his wife wrote the booking of every trip in a register and kept a ticket from each town they came to. The card inside the cover is my grandfather's, and the essay at the back was written by a schoolboy. Every page is thin and dry, and the words on them have lasted much longer than the boat did.","zh":"每年冬天我都读一本关于海的书。那不是小说，而是一个在船上干了三十年的人的记录。他起初握不住笔，所以他妻子把每次出航的登记都写进一本登记簿，还留下他们到过的每个城镇的船票。封面里那张卡片是我祖父的，后面那篇文章是一个小学生写的。"},"case":{"tw":[["casing",4],["cause",0],["box",3],["problem",2],["trial",6],["slip",0],["face",0],["pack",3]],"en":"In this case there is no easy answer. The problem is not the box; it is the casing inside it, which is thin. Nobody can find the cause. At the trial the judge asked for a slip of paper with the numbers on it, and my face gave me away. I had to pack the whole thing again and take it home on the bus. The next case on the list was even worse. Two weeks later a man came to the door with the same box and asked me the same question again.","zh":"这个案子里没有简单的答案。问题不在箱子，而在里面那层很薄的壳体。没人找得出原因。开审时法官要一张写有数字的纸条，而我的脸色把我出卖了。我只好把东西重新打包，坐公交带回家。清单上的下一个案子更糟。"},"class":{"tw":[["classify",4],["course",0],["count",3],["league",2],["standard",6],["family",0],["rank",6],["form",0]],"en":"Our class has twenty-two children in it. The teacher has to classify them by age and by reading level, and the standard of the older ones is not much higher. We play in a small league on Saturdays, and my rank in the group is fourth. The course lasts one year. The form of the test has changed twice since I came. In my family nobody finished school, so I count myself lucky to be here at all. The teacher says a good class is not a list of names but a habit of working that lasts for years.","zh":"我们班有二十二个孩子。老师得按年龄和阅读水平给他们分类，而大孩子的水平并不高多少。我们周六参加一个小联赛，我在组里的名次是第四。课程为期一年。我入学以来考试的形式已经改过两次。我们家没人读完过中学，所以我觉得自己能在这儿已经很幸运了。"},"country":{"tw":[["rural",4],["land",0],["open",3],["region",2],["nation",0],["state",0],["far",6],["space",3]],"en":"I grew up in the country, in a rural region where the land is cheap and the roads are empty. Our nation has eight such regions, and the state pays for the schools in all of them. The open field behind our house is the only space the children have. The nearest town is far; my aunt says it takes an hour if the wind is against you. In summer the whole country smells of cut grass. The government sends one bus a week, and the driver knows every family in the valley by name.","zh":"我在乡下长大，那是个土地便宜、道路空旷的农业地区。我们国家有八个这样的地区，所有地区的学校都由政府出资。屋后那片开阔的田是孩子们仅有的空间。最近的镇子很远；我姑妈说，要是逆风得走一个小时。夏天整个乡下都是青草被割过的味道。"},"act":{"tw":[["begin",3],["serve",2],["refrain",1],["move",0],["deal",3],["event",2],["order",6],["play",0]],"en":"The act begins at seven. First they serve the soup, then the play starts, and nobody may move from their seat. I have to deal with the last table and give the order to the kitchen before the second act. Please refrain from talking during the music. The whole event lasts two hours, and by the end my feet are dead. The same thing happens every Friday, and I still enjoy it. The young woman who plays the mother has never acted before, and she is very good. After the last curtain we wash the glasses and count the money.","zh":"这幕戏七点开始。先上汤，然后戏才开演，谁都不许离开座位。我得收拾最后一张桌子，并在第二幕之前把点单送进厨房。音乐响起时请勿交谈。整个活动持续两小时，结束时我的脚都站麻了。每周五都是这样，而我依然挺喜欢。"},"add":{"tw":[["bring",0],["subtract",1],["combine",6],["total",0],["include",3],["count",2],["extra",6],["contribute",0]],"en":"Please add these two figures and bring me the total. You may not subtract anything, and you must include the extra charge for delivery. If you combine the two lists, the count will be wrong by one. Everyone in the office had to contribute a little. I checked it twice before I took it in, and the answer looked simple to everybody. The figures come from two different books, and each one has its own way of counting. If the total is not the same in both, we start again from the beginning.","zh":"请把这两个数字加起来，把总数拿来给我。不许减掉任何一项，还必须把额外的运费算进去。如果把两张清单合并，计数就会差一个。办公室里每个人都得出一点力。我交上去之前核了两遍，而在所有人看来答案都显而易见。"},"agree":{"tw":[["check",0],["accept",2],["disagree",1],["consider",6],["fit",0],["meet",3],["suit",2],["negotiate",6]],"en":"I agree with you about the price, but I cannot accept the date. We can meet on Thursday and negotiate the rest. Let me check the small room first; if the table does not fit, the whole plan is no good. Consider the other offer before you decide. My brother disagrees with me and says the later date would suit him much better. He wants the later date because his son will be home from the army by then. That is a good reason, and I have no good reason of my own.","zh":"价钱上我同意你，但日期我不能接受。我们周四见面，其余的事再谈。先让我看看那间小屋；桌子放不下的话，整个计划就不行。做决定前你也考虑一下另一个报价。我哥哥不同意我，他说晚一点那个日期对他合适得多。"},"allow":{"tw":[["admit",3],["accept",2],["deny",1],["require",6],["trust",3],["assign",2],["enable",6],["grant",0]],"en":"They do not allow dogs in the shop. The sign says they cannot admit animals, and they deny that it has anything to do with the owner. Anyone who wants to bring one must accept the rule. The job will require an hour of training, and the manager will assign somebody to help you. This small key will enable you to open the back door. I trust they will grant us one more week. The shop next door allows them, and half the street goes there instead. The owner says he will not change his mind, and I believe him.","zh":"他们不许带狗进店。牌子上说不能接纳动物，他们否认这与主人有关。想带狗来的人必须接受这条规矩。这份活需要一小时培训，经理会指派一个人帮你。这把小钥匙能让你打开后门。我相信他们会再宽限我们一周。"},"answer":{"tw":[["reply",2],["field",3],["meet",2],["question",1],["serve",3],["counter",3],["state",2],["result",0]],"en":"I wrote my answer and put it on the counter. There was no reply for a week, and then a short letter came. The state of the field is the real question here: nobody can meet in a wet meadow, and the result would be a mess. I asked again at the second window, and the woman there could not serve me either. So I went home and waited for the third letter. In the third week I met the owner himself at the door of the office. He answered every question except the one I had actually asked.","zh":"我把答案写好放在柜台上。一周都没有回音，然后来了一封短信。这里的真正问题是场地状况：没人能在湿草地里集会，结果只会一团糟。我又到第二个窗口去问，那里的女士也帮不了我。于是我回家等第三封信。"},"bottom":{"tw":[["bed",0],["base",3],["hit",2],["side",2],["spot",6],["behind",0],["foot",3],["land",2],["plate",6]],"en":"At the bottom of the garden there is a bed of stones. The base of the old wall is under it, and on the far side you can see a plate of iron fixed into the ground. We used to hit it with a stick when we were children. The spot behind the tree is where my dog liked to sleep. From there you can put your foot on the land beyond the fence. In summer the whole garden smells of wet stone, and the bed under the wall is the coolest place in it.","zh":"园子最底下有一片石头地。那堵旧墙的基座就在下面，靠外的一侧能看到一块嵌进地里的铁板。我们小时候常拿棍子敲它。树后那一处是我家狗爱睡的地方。从那儿你可以把脚伸到栅栏外的土地上去。"},"break":{"tw":[["blow",3],["change",2],["repair",1],["check",0],["chip",3],["dance",2],["die",0],["back",6]],"en":"Take a break at four; you look tired. A single blow from that hammer can chip the stone, and the break in the wall will only get worse. Nobody can repair it in one day, and a small change here will not help. Check the back of the house first, where the wind comes in. The old tree will die this year. Come and dance with me instead; the wall has waited thirty years. The crack runs from the window down to the floor, and in winter it lets the cold air in.","zh":"四点歇一下吧，你看上去累了。那把锤子敲一下就能把石头崩出缺口，而墙上的裂口只会越来越大。一天之内谁也修不好，在这里做点小改动也没用。先去查看房子背面，风是从那儿灌进来的。那棵老树今年会死。不如过来跟我跳舞吧，那堵墙等了三十年了。"},"change":{"tw":[["alter",0],["break",3],["dress",2],["stay",1],["exchange",0],["cut",3],["travel",2],["reason",6],["shift",0]],"en":"You cannot change this without asking. Nothing can alter the size of the door, and if you cut the frame you will break the glass. There is a good reason for the rule: the shift of the wind in winter is strong enough to travel through any small gap. I had to dress in two coats and stay inside. In the future we will exchange the old panes for new ones. Anything you alter in this room has to be written in the book by the door. The book has been there for a hundred years and the handwriting is very small.","zh":"不打招呼你不能改动这里。门的尺寸无法更改，要是削了框子就会打碎玻璃。这条规定有它的道理：冬天风向一变，风大得能从任何小缝里钻进来。我不得不穿上两件外套待在屋里。以后我们会把旧玻璃换成新的。"},"clean":{"tw":[["clear",0],["wash",3],["change",2],["dirty",1],["enough",6],["fair",5],["brush",3],["remove",2],["water",6],["fresh",0]],"en":"Keep the room clean: wash the floor, brush the table and remove every plate before you leave. The water in the bucket must be clear, not fresh, and the cloth has to be clean enough to use twice. If the sheets are dirty, change them. It is not fair to leave that work to the next person. I have done it for eleven years, and the room has never once been dirty on my shift. When the shift ends I put the brushes back in the cupboard and lock it. The next person will find everything exactly where it belongs.","zh":"把屋子保持干净：走之前擦地、刷桌、把所有盘子收走。桶里的水要清，不必是新打的；抹布得干净到还能再用一次。床单脏了就换。把活儿留给下一个人是不公平的。我干了十一年，我班上这屋子从没脏过。"},"comfort":{"tw":[["ease",0],["calm",3],["aid",2],["discomfort",1],["sense",6],["console",0],["relief",3],["condition",2]],"en":"The old chair gives me more comfort than the new one. It has a calm shape and a soft cushion, and when my back is bad it is a real aid. The discomfort in my knees goes away within a minute of sitting down. My only sense of relief in the evening comes from that chair. My sister tries to console me by saying it is an ordinary chair, but she does not have to sit in it all day. For ease of mind I have written its condition on a card and hung the card on the back of the chair.","zh":"那把旧椅子比新的更让我舒服。它形制沉静、坐垫柔软，我背痛的时候它真帮得上忙。一坐下不到一分钟，膝盖的不适就消失了。晚上我唯一的放松感就来自那把椅子。我妹妹想安慰我，说那只是把普通的椅子，可她不用整天坐在上面。"},"continue":{"tw":[["cover",0],["carry",3],["act",2],["discontinue",1],["bring",6],["stay",0],["cross",3],["talk",2],["extend",0],["move",6]],"en":"We will continue the work tomorrow. Nobody can carry on like this: two of the men have gone home and the rain shows no sign of stopping. Every act of repair here begins in the rain. If they discontinue the service, we will have to cover the roof ourselves and stay until it is done. I cannot talk about it any longer. Let us cross the yard, move the boxes inside, and then we will extend the plan by a week. Somebody has to bring the tarpaulin before the night shift starts.","zh":"明天我们继续干。没人能这样撑下去：两个人已经回家了，雨也没有要停的样子。这里每一次修理都是在雨里开的头。要是他们停掉这项服务，我们就得自己盖屋顶，一直干完为止。我不能再聊这个了。我们穿过院子，把箱子搬进屋，然后把这个计划延长一周。"},"air":{"tw":[["aerial",4],["line",0],["breath",3],["dry",2],["light",6],["aerate",4],["send",0],["note",3],["gas",2],["jet",6],["atmosphere",0]],"en":"The small radio station sits on a hill where the air is dry and clear. Every morning the engineer opens the windows to aerate the room before the first show. She sends the signal along one line to a tall aerial on the roof, and from there it travels by jet to towns far away. The music she plays has a simple air, a tune you can hum note by note. The light from her desk lamp is the only other thing in the room. She takes a deep breath, waits for the gas heater to warm the air, and thinks about the wide atmosphere outside.","zh":"那座小电台坐落在山丘上，那儿的空气又干又清。每天早上，工程师都要打开窗户，让直播间的空气流通一下，然后才开始第一档节目。她把信号顺着一条线路送到屋顶那根高高的天线上，再从那里传往很远的小镇。她放的音乐调子很简单，是可以一个音符一个音符哼出来的。书桌台灯的光是屋里唯一另外的亮处。她深吸一口气，等着煤气取暖器把空气烘暖，心里想着外面那一片广阔的天地。"},"cry":{"tw":[["call",0],["noise",3],["change",2],["laugh",1],["remember",6],["shout",0],["tear",3],["express",2],["wonder",6],["scream",3]],"en":"When the baby began to cry, my sister did not shout or scream. She picked him up and made a low sound, a kind of call that he seemed to remember from another night. The noise in the flat was terrible, so she took him to the window for a change of air. He would laugh, then cry again, and a single tear ran down his cheek. I wonder how a small child can express so much with one sound. She said that all mothers learn it, and that she would remember it for the rest of her life.","zh":"孩子一哭，我姐姐既没有喊也没有尖叫。她把他抱起来，发出一个很低的声音，像是某种呼唤，他好像记得这是从别的夜里听过的。屋里的噪声糟透了，她抱他到窗边换换空气。他笑一下，又哭起来，一滴眼泪顺着脸颊往下流。我奇怪一个这么小的孩子怎么能用一声哭表达这么多。她说当妈的都会这一手，她一辈子都会记得。"},"cat":{"tw":[["feline",4],["guy",0],["man",2],["dog",6],["sick",0],["woman",2],["rabbit",6],["cast",0]],"en":"The woman next door keeps a cat that has never once been friendly to me. She says it is a feline thing, and that a dog would be easier, but she is fond of it. There is a man down the road who swears he saw it cast a shadow on the wall like a person. Once, when the animal was sick, she would not leave the house for a week. My brother, who is a quiet guy, says the rabbit in our garden is the reason it comes over our fence so often.","zh":"隔壁那位女士养了一只猫，那猫从来没对我友好过。她说这是猫的天性，还说养条狗会省事些，可她就是喜欢它。路那头有个男人一口咬定，说他见过这猫在墙上投下一个像人一样的影子。有一回这猫病了，她整整一个星期没出门。我弟弟是个安静的人，他说我们园子里那只兔子，就是它总翻过篱笆过来的原因。"},"cause":{"tw":[["causal",4],["drive",0],["bring",3],["origin",2],["risk",6],["engine",3],["venture",2],["result",6]],"en":"Nobody could say what the cause of the fire had been. The engine of the old car was cold, and there was no sign of anyone in the yard. My father said the most likely origin was a wire under the floor, though he admitted that was only a guess. He would not risk another night in the house, so he asked me to drive to my aunt's. She asked him to bring the papers with him, and he did not venture an opinion again until the morning. The result of the inquiry was the same: no clear reason. He said a causal chain like that is easy to see afterwards and impossible to see at the time.","zh":"没人说得清那场火是因何而起的。旧车的发动机是凉的，院子里也没有人来过的痕迹。我爸说最可能起头的地方是地板下的一根电线，不过他也承认这只是猜的。他不肯再在这屋里冒险住一晚，于是我们开车去了姑姑家。她叫他把文件带上，他一晚上没再开口说什么，直到第二天早上。查问的结果还是一样：没有明确的原因。他说，这样的因果链，事后看得清，当时看不见。"},"dress":{"tw":[["dresser",4],["clip",0],["change",3],["cook",2],["wear",6],["coat",3],["finish",2],["attire",6]],"en":"My mother would dress for dinner even when there was nobody to see her. She would change out of her working clothes, clip her hair back, and put on a dark coat. She would wear the same one for twenty years. Her attire never changed with fashion. Then she would cook, and the finish of the meal always mattered more to her than the dress itself. The dresser in her room still holds the same things: a comb, a pin, and a photograph of her mother in a dress of pale blue.","zh":"哪怕没人看，我妈吃晚饭也要换身体面的衣服。她脱下干活的衣裳，把头发别上去，再穿上一件深色外套。同一件她一穿就是二十年。她的穿戴从不跟着时兴走。然后她去做饭，而对她来说，一顿饭最后收得好不好，比身上这条裙子要紧得多。她房里的梳妆台里还是那几样东西：一把梳子、一根别针，还有一张她母亲穿浅蓝裙子的照片。"},"address":{"tw":[["call",0],["ask",3],["use",2],["message",6],["cover",0],["approach",3],["access",2],["public",6],["deal",0]],"en":"The chairman had to address a room of two hundred people, and he was not used to it. He would call a name, ask a question, and then wait too long for an answer. His message was simple, but he had to cover a great deal of ground before he came to it. He had no access to the figures, so he had to approach the problem from the side. It was a public meeting, and by the end even the people at the back had understood what he wanted.","zh":"主席得对着一屋子两百号人讲话，他不习惯这个。他会点一个名字，问一个问题，然后等答案等得太久。他要说的其实很简单，可走到正题之前得铺陈好大一片。他手头没有数据，只好从侧面去谈这个问题。那是一场公开的会，到散场时，连最后一排的人也知道他要的是什么了。"},"ask":{"tw":[["need",0],["call",3],["address",2],["tell",6],["demand",2],["cost",3],["communicate",2],["want",6],["require",0]],"en":"If you need to ask a favour of my father, you should call him in the evening and tell him plainly what you want. He does not like a long speech. He will demand to know the cost before he agrees to anything, and he will require you to say when you need it. He is not easy to address on the phone, because he does not like to communicate in that way. But once he has said yes, he will not go back on it. That, to him, is what an honest answer means.","zh":"你要是有事求我爸，就在晚上给他打电话，直截了当跟他说你要什么。他不爱听长篇大论。答应任何事之前，他都要先问清代价，还得让你说准什么时候要。在电话里跟他说话不容易，因为他不喜欢用这种方式交流。可一旦他点头，就不会反悔。在他看来，说一句实在话就是这个意思。"},"ball":{"tw":[["egg",0],["football",3],["dance",2],["kick",6],["lump",0],["bowl",3],["wind",2],["catch",6],["formal",0]],"en":"My cousin played football every Saturday and could catch almost anything with one hand. Before a game he would eat two eggs and a bowl of rice, and then kick a ball against the wall for an hour. After the game there was a dance at the club, and he had to wear something formal for it, which he hated. He was never good at that side of things. In a hard wind he would stand with his hands in his pockets and roll a small lump of bread between his fingers.","zh":"我表哥每个星期六都踢球，几乎什么东西单手都能接住。比赛前他会吃两个鸡蛋、一碗米饭，然后对着墙踢一个小时球。比赛结束后俱乐部有舞会，他得穿点正式的衣裳，他讨厌这个。这方面他从来不行。刮大风的时候，他就把手插在兜里站着，指头间搓着一小块面包。"},"bar":{"tw":[["cake",0],["close",3],["room",2],["shop",6],["stop",0],["save",3],["support",2],["block",2]],"en":"There is a small bar at the corner of our street, and the man who keeps it knows everyone. He will close the shop at eleven, wipe the bar, and put a cake under a glass cover for the morning. People come in to stop for a while and talk about the weather in the back room. He has one rule: if you cannot support yourself on the stool, you have had enough. In winter the snow can block the door, and he will not let anyone save him the trouble of clearing it himself.","zh":"我们街角有个小酒吧，看店的那个人认识所有人。他十一点打烊，把吧台擦干净，再把一块蛋糕搁在玻璃罩下留着早上。人们进来歇一会儿，在里屋聊聊天气。他有一条规矩：你要是坐都坐不稳，那就是喝够了。冬天下雪能把门堵住，他不让别人替他省这份力气，自己扫。"},"bear":{"tw":[["accept",3],["deal",3],["act",2],["bull",1],["little",6],["birth",0],["drop",3],["big",6],["carry",3]],"en":"There was a bear in the woods above the village that summer, a big one with a little cub. The farmers would not accept it; they said it would deal with the sheep the way a bull deals with a fence. My father had to act fast, so he and two others went up with a lamp and a gun. They did not shoot. They watched the mother carry her cub across the stream and drop into the dark on the far side. He said afterwards that he had seen a birth and a death in the same minute, and that he would not go up there again.","zh":"那年夏天，村子上头的林子里来了一只熊，个头很大，带着一只小崽。种地的人不肯认这事，说它对付羊就像公牛对付栅栏一样。我爸得赶紧行动，于是他和另外两个人提着灯、带着枪上了山。他们没有开枪。他们看着母熊把小崽叼过溪水，落到对岸的黑地里去。事后他说，他在同一分钟里看见了生和死，以后再也不上去了。"},"beat":{"tw":[["dead",0],["full",3],["move",2],["upset",6],["pound",0],["kill",3],["play",2],["win",6],["round",0]],"en":"You could hear the beat of the drum from the far end of the field. It was a full band, and the players had to move with the music or lose the round. My brother was upset before the match; he said his legs felt dead and heavy. He began to pound the ball against the wall to warm up, and after ten minutes he could play again. In the last minute they managed to win, and the crowd made a noise like a heart beating. It was the sort of afternoon that could kill a man's nerve, and he came through it.","zh":"从场地那头就能听见鼓点。那是个满编的乐队，球员得跟着音乐动，不然这一轮就丢了。比赛前我弟弟心里发慌，他说两条腿又沉又死。他开始对着墙猛砸球热身，十分钟以后又能踢了。最后一分钟他们赢了，看台上的声浪像心跳一样。那种下午最能毁掉一个人的胆气，而他从里面走了出来。"},"bed":{"tw":[["bottom",0],["course",3],["plant",2],["room",6],["love",0],["lift",3],["supply",2],["bare",6],["bang",0]],"en":"The bed in my room stood under the window, and in summer I could see the bottom of the garden from it. Of course it was too small for me by the time I was fifteen, and my feet hung over the end. On the far side there was a bare wall where my mother had tried to plant a rose that never grew. She would lift the mattress every spring to air it, and she kept a small supply of clean sheets in a box underneath. In winter the wind would bang the shutter against the frame all night, and I would love it.","zh":"我屋里的床摆在窗下，夏天我能从床上看见园子的尽头。当然，到我十五岁它就太小了，脚都搭在床沿外。对面是一堵光墙，我妈曾在那儿试着种一棵玫瑰，没活。每年春天她都会把床垫抬起来晾一晾，床底下的箱子里存着一小摞干净床单。冬天风整夜把窗板拍在框上，我倒很喜欢。"},"bill":{"tw":[["card",0],["check",3],["advertise",2],["repeal",6],["charge",0],["menu",3],["list",2],["tax",6],["note",0]],"en":"The bill came to more than we had expected, and my father asked to see the menu again. He would check every item on the list, note the charge for the bread, and then take out his card. The owner had begun to advertise a new tax on the board outside, and my father said a good council would repeal it within the year. He paid without another word and left the note on the table. On the way home he told me that a bill is a promise written down, and that it should be read twice.","zh":"账单比我们预想的高，我爸要求再看一遍菜单。他把单子上的每一顶都核了一遍，记下面包收的那笔钱，然后掏出卡。店主已经在外面板子上开始宣传一项新税，我爸说，一个像样的议会一年之内就会把它废掉。他一句话没说就付了钱，纸条留在桌上。回家路上他跟我说，账单就是写下来的承诺，得读两遍。"},"blow":{"tw":[["snow",0],["box",3],["lay",2],["attempt",6],["waste",0],["burn",3],["move",2],["pull",6],["bump",0]],"en":"The wind began to blow hard in the night and the snow came with it. In the morning the whole lane was under a white cover, and my father had to pull on his boots and move the car out of the way. There was a bump in the road that nobody could see, and it took him three attempts to get past it. He would burn the old boxes in the yard rather than waste them, and then lay a plank over the gap so the milkman could get through.","zh":"夜里起大风，雪跟着来了。早上整条小路都盖在白色底下一层，我爸只好蹬上靴子把车挪开。路上有个谁都看不见的坎，他试了三回才过去。他宁可把旧木箱在院子里烧掉，也不肯白白扔了，然后铺一块板子盖住坑，好让送牛奶的能过。"},"bother":{"tw":[["pain",0],["harass",3],["affect",2],["guess",6],["trouble",0],["plague",3],["confuse",2],["hurry",6],["devil",0]],"en":"It did not bother my grandmother that the tap dripped all night; she said a small trouble was better than a silent house. The pain in her knee would affect her in the mornings, and she would have to hurry less than she wanted to. I guess she was lonely, though she would never say so. The neighbours began to harass her about the garden, and one of them, a real devil of a man, would plague her every week. It only seemed to confuse her that anyone should mind so much.","zh":"水龙头整夜滴水，我奶奶一点不烦；她说有点小麻烦总比静得没声的屋子好。早上膝盖的疼会影响她，她想赶也赶不起来。我猜她是孤单的，虽然她从不这么说。邻居开始为园子的事来烦她，其中有个真像恶鬼一样的男人，每个星期都来缠她。别人这么在意，反倒让她摸不着头脑。"},"bring":{"tw":[["add",0],["return",3],["change",2],["help",6],["land",3],["fetch",3],["attract",2],["need",6],["play",0]],"en":"Every Sunday my uncle would bring the boat back to the harbour and bring the nets with him. He would return the key to the office, add a line to the list on the wall, and then fetch his bicycle. The land around the harbour had begun to change, and the new houses would attract people who had no need of a boat at all. He said he would help anyone who asked, but he would not play along with the council. In the end he sold up and moved inland.","zh":"每个星期天，我叔都把船带回港里，顺便把网也带回来。他把钥匙还给办公室，在墙上那张单子上添一行，然后去取自行车。港口周围的地开始变了，新盖的房子会招来那些根本用不着船的人。他说谁开口求他他都帮，但他不陪着镇公所作戏。最后他把东西都卖了，搬到了内地。"},"build":{"tw":[["figure",0],["lock",3],["better",2],["construct",6],["form",0],["raise",3],["body",2],["develop",6],["shape",0]],"en":"They had to build the new shed before the winter, and there was little time. The figure on the plan was simple, but nobody could agree on the form it should take. They would raise the walls first, then lock the two halves together with a long bar. My father said they would have to develop the design as they went, and change its shape twice before it was right. In the end the body of the shed was stronger than the old house, and better built, too. He had watched men construct barns all his life, and he knew that a good frame is never hurried.","zh":"他们得在入冬前把新棚子盖起来，时间不多。图上的尺寸很简单，可谁也说不准该做成什么形状。他们先把墙立起来，再用一根长杆把两半锁在一起。我爸说设计得边干边改，形状换了两回才对。最后棚子的主体比那栋老房子还结实，活儿也干得更好。他这辈子看着人盖谷仓，知道好架子从来不是赶出来的。"},"burn":{"tw":[["cut",0],["flame",3],["feel",2],["smoke",6],["fire",0],["blaze",3],["pain",2],["tear",6],["bite",0]],"en":"The fire in the field began to burn along the dry grass and the smoke could be seen from the road. My uncle had to cut a strip of ground to stop it, and by the time he had finished he could feel the heat through his boots. A single flame had started the whole blaze. He had a bad burn on one hand, and the pain kept him awake. It made his eyes tear. He said it was nothing, but he could not hold a cup without biting his lip.","zh":"地里的火顺着干草烧起来，从路上就能看见烟。我叔得先割出一条空地把它拦住，等他割完，隔着靴子都能感觉到烫。整场大火是从一簇火苗起的。他一只手烧伤了，疼得整夜睡不着，眼睛都给熏出泪来。他说没事，可是端起杯子就忍不住咬嘴唇。"},"call":{"tw":[["address",2],["bet",3],["ask",2],["answer",6],["cry",0],["double",3],["guess",2],["talk",6],["promise",0]],"en":"My father had to make one call and then he would leave the office. He asked for the number, gave his address, and waited for an answer. Then he had a long talk with a man he had worked with for years, and they made a bet about which of them would retire first. He could not guess his own luck well enough to double the stake. As he put the phone down he heard a cry from the street. He had promised to be home by six, and it was already past six.","zh":"我爸打完一个电话就要下班了。他问了号码，报了自己的地址，等着对方接。接着他跟一个共事多年的男人聊了很久，两人还打赌看谁先退休。他摸不准自己的运气，不敢把赌注翻倍。放下电话时，他听见街上一声喊叫。他早就答应六点前到家，可已经过六点了。"},"can":{"tw":[["behind",0],["head",3],["room",2],["able",6],["bottom",0],["retire",3],["remove",2],["need",6],["fire",0]],"en":"The can of paint stood at the bottom of the shelf behind the door, and nobody in the room seemed able to reach it. My grandfather would need a ladder, or he would have to remove the boxes in front. He would not retire until he had done the job himself, and he was not going to ask anyone. He put his head round the corner, took a long breath, and lifted the can down. There is no need for a fire, he said. It is only paint. Then he carried it out to the yard.","zh":"那罐油漆放在门后架子的最下层，屋里好像谁也没本事够到它。我爷爷要么得找把梯子，要么得把前面的箱子挪开。活儿没自己干完他是不肯收手的，也不打算开口求人。他把头探过拐角，长吸一口气，把那罐子端了下来。他说：用不着生火，就是油漆而已。然后他把它拎到院子里去了。"},"care":{"tw":[["charge",0],["mother",3],["control",2],["benefit",6],["concern",0],["nurse",3],["help",2],["medical",6],["deal",0]],"en":"My mother gave up her job to take care of my grandmother, and she did it for six years. She would deal with the nurse every morning, and she knew more about the medical side of it than any of the doctors. She had to control her own worry, because my grandmother could read a face at once. Her only concern was that the old woman should not feel a burden. She said there was no charge for what she did, and no benefit she wanted out of it. I never heard her ask anyone for help.","zh":"我妈辞了工作去照顾我奶奶，一照顾就是六年。每天早上她跟护士打交道，对这病医药方面的事，比哪个大夫都清楚。她还得管住自己的担心，因为我奶奶一眼就能看出人脸上的心思。她唯一在意的是别让老太太觉得自己是个累赘。她说她做的事不要钱，也不图什么好处。我从没听她开口求过谁帮忙。"},"chance":{"tw":[["find",0],["room",3],["try",2],["opportunity",6],["happen",0],["say",3],["measure",2],["hope",6],["luck",0]],"en":"There was a chance that the shop would close, and I wanted to find out before it happened. I went in and asked, and the woman said she would try to keep it open for another year. The room at the back was full of old stock, and the opportunity to sell it was small. You have to measure your hope, she said, and then take the luck that comes. I did not know what to say. I bought a book and left, and I still go back when I can.","zh":"这家店有可能要关，我想在它关掉之前弄清楚。我进去问了，那位女士说她会尽量再撑一年。里屋堆满了旧货，能卖出去的机会不大。她说：希望得掂量着来，然后来了运气就接住。我不知道该说什么。我买了一本书就走了，到现在有机会还回去看看。"},"charge":{"tw":[["bill",0],["bother",3],["change",2],["discharge",1],["criminal",6],["care",0],["check",3],["cost",2],["excite",0]],"en":"The charge against the man was serious, and nobody in the village wanted to talk about it. He was said to have set fire to a shop over a bill he could not pay, though the whole cost was small. The police had to discharge the case for lack of proof, and the criminal court never saw it. The change in the town afterwards was strange: people who had not bothered to speak to him before began to care what happened. I was excited and ashamed at the same time. My father told me to check my own books first.","zh":"对那个人的指控不轻，村里谁都不愿提这事。据说他为一笔付不起的账放火烧了一家店，其实总共也没多少钱。因为证据不足，警方只好撤了案，刑事法庭根本没审。之后镇上的变化很怪：先前连话都懒得跟他说的人，忽然开始关心起他的下场。我既兴奋又羞愧。我爸叫我先把自己那本账查清楚。"},"check":{"tw":[["agree",0],["card",3],["bill",2],["notice",6],["break",0],["catch",3],["change",2],["collect",6],["chip",0]],"en":"Before we paid, my mother would check the bill twice and then check it again. She would agree to nothing until she had seen the card in the window with the prices on it. There was a small notice by the door, and she read it while I waited. If the figures did not change, she would collect her bag and walk out without a word. My brother said she had a chip of ice where other people keep their patience. I took it as a break from the heat, and I did not catch her eye.","zh":"付钱之前，我妈要把账单核对两遍，然后再核一遍。没看见窗户上那张写着价钱的牌子，她什么都不会答应。门边有一张小告示，我等着的时候她把它读完了。数目要是不改，她就收拾起包，一声不响走出去。我弟说她身上那块地方别人都长着耐心，她长的是一块冰。我只当这是热天里歇口气，没敢跟她对上眼。"},"chip":{"tw":[["bit",0],["scale",3],["cut",2],["computer",6],["check",0],["splinter",3],["shape",2],["micro",6],["crisp",0]],"en":"There was a chip in the glass, a small bit of it missing at the edge, and it had a strange shape. I had to check it against the scale on the wall before I could say how deep the cut went. My father said the whole thing would break if we left it, so he took a splinter of wood and worked at it. He had a computer in the back room, and he used it to look up the price. A micro part of the surface was all that mattered. He said a crisp new one would cost too much.","zh":"玻璃上崩了一块，边上缺了小小一角，形状还挺怪。我得对着墙上的标尺量一下，才说得清那道口子有多深。我爸说这么放着整块都会裂，于是他拿了一根木片慢慢修。里屋有台电脑，他用它查了价钱。要紧的就是表面上极小的那一块。他说换一块又新又脆的要花太多钱。"},"clear":{"tw":[["clean",0],["approve",3],["change",2],["bounce",1],["without",6],["light",0],["commission",3],["empty",2],["open",0]],"en":"The water in the tank was clear again, and you could see the bottom of it in the light from the door. The man from the water commission came to approve the change we had made, and he said the whole job was clean work. He had to bounce a stone off the wall to test how hard it was. The room was empty except for a chair. We cannot go on without a proper cover, he said. Leave the lid open when you are finished. I wrote it down and he signed the paper.","zh":"水箱里的水又清了，顺着门口透进来的光能看见箱底。自来水委员会的那个人来查看我们做的改动，说这活儿干得干净。他用一块石头在墙上弹了一下，试试墙有多硬。屋里除了一把椅子什么都没有。他说：没有个像样的盖子，这么下去不行。收工的时候把盖子敞着。我记了下来，他在纸上签了字。"},"colour":{"tw":[["distort",0],["blue",3],["change",2],["palette",6],["gloss",0],["green",3],["interest",2],["bright",6],["tinge",0]],"en":"The colour of the sea changes ten times in a day, and no painter can hold it. My aunt would put a blue and a green on her palette and then add a tinge of grey, and by the afternoon the whole canvas had gone wrong. A photograph can distort what you saw, she said, and a gloss will hide the rest. Her real interest was in the light, not in the paint. The bright hours on the water were the ones she wanted. I watched her work for a whole summer and still cannot say how she did it.","zh":"海的颜色一天能变十回，哪个画画的都抓不住。我姑姑会在调色板上挤一坨蓝、一坨绿，再添一丝灰，到下午整幅画就全不对了。她说：照片会把你看见的东西扭歪，再上一层亮油就把剩下的都盖住了。她真正上心的是光，不是颜料。水面上那几段亮堂堂的时辰才是她想要的。我看她画了一整个夏天，到现在也说不出她是怎么画的。"},"company":{"tw":[["party",0],["chorus",3],["unit",2],["firm",6],["society",0],["cohort",3],["complement",2],["subsidiary",6],["accompany",0]],"en":"My father worked for a small firm for most of his life, and he was happy there. The company had one unit in the north and a subsidiary in another town, and he would have to accompany the manager on the long drive between them. At the office party each winter the whole cohort would stand up and sing in a chorus, badly. He said there was no better society than people who work well together. When a new man joined, my father told him he was a useful complement to the team, and meant it.","zh":"我爸大半辈子在一家小事务所做事，在那儿过得挺开心。这家公司北边有一个部门，另一个镇上还有家子公司，他得陪着经理在两头之间开长途。每年冬天公司聚会上，他们那一拨人都会站起来合唱，唱得很难听。他说再没有比一起把活干好的人更好的群体了。来了新人的时候，我爸会跟他说他是队里缺的那一块，而且是真心这么说的。"},"complete":{"tw":[["finish",0],["close",3],["end",2],["full",6],["over",0],["top",3],["fill",2],["entire",6],["perfect",0]],"en":"The work on the house was complete by the middle of June, and the whole family came to see it. We had to finish the top floor last, and it took a week to fill the gaps and close every door properly. The entire roof was new, and over the gate my father had put a small stone with the date on it. He said the house was not perfect, but it was full of light and it was ours. At the end of the day we sat in the yard and watched the sun go down.","zh":"房子到六月中就完工了，全家人都来看。顶楼是最后收的尾，光补缝、把每扇门关严实就用了一个星期。整个屋顶都是新的，大门上方我爸嵌了块小石头，上面刻着日期。他说这房子算不上十全十美，可是光线足，而且是咱们自己的。那天傍晚我们坐在院子里看太阳落下去。"},"concern":{"tw":[["care",0],["involve",3],["anxiety",2],["impact",6],["fear",0],["matter",3],["enterprise",2],["strong",6],["interest",2]],"en":"My uncle's only concern was that the enterprise should outlive him. He had built it from nothing, and he would involve himself in every small matter, from the price of wood to the colour of the sign. His anxiety before each winter was strong, and I came to share his fear of a bad season. He used to say that the impact of one bad year can undo ten good ones. He did not care much for money, but he cared a great deal about the interest of the people who worked for him.","zh":"我叔唯一放心不下的是这份事业得比他活得久。他是从一无所有把它做起来的，事无大小都要自己插手，从木料的价钱到招牌的颜色。每年入冬前他都格外焦虑，我也跟着他一起怕遇上坏年景。他生前常说，一个坏年头的折腾能把十个好年头搭进去。他对钱不怎么在意，可对跟着他干活那些人的利害，他上心得很。"},"control":{"tw":[["check",0],["card",3],["power",2],["system",6],["hold",0],["catch",3],["test",2],["force",6],["insure",0]],"en":"The control room was small and hot, and there was a card on the wall with the names of everyone who had ever worked there. You had to check the board every hour, and if a light went red you had to catch it at once. The whole system depended on one man keeping his hold on himself. The power came from two old wheels in the river below. A sudden force of water could test the best of them. They would insure the building against fire, but nothing could insure a man against his own temper. My father learned that in his first year and never forgot it.","zh":"控制室又小又热，墙上钉着一张卡片，写着所有在这儿干过活的人的名字。你得每小时查一次仪表盘，哪个灯变红了就得马上发现。整套系统全靠一个人把自己稳住。电从下面河里的两只旧水轮来。水势猛地一冲，最能干的人也经不住考。他们会给这楼保火险，可谁也没法给一个人的脾气保险。我爸头一年就懂了这一点，一辈子没忘。"},"cook":{"tw":[["fix",0],["brown",3],["change",2],["curry",6],["prepare",0],["dress",3],["cheat",2],["lamb",6],["ready",0]],"en":"My mother could cook anything, even a curry that my father said was the best he had ever eaten. She would prepare the lamb the night before, dress it with salt and herbs, and let it stand. In the morning she would brown it in a heavy pan and then change the heat. I used to fix the table while she worked, and I was never ready when she called. She said a cook who cheats with the timing will always be caught by the taste. Once a week she would let me stir the pot and tell me what to look for.","zh":"我妈什么都会做，有一道咖喱我爸说他一辈子没吃过更好的。她会头天晚上就把羊肉备好，撒上盐和香料，放着入味。第二天早上用厚锅把肉煎上色，再调火。她做饭的时候我就摆桌子，可每次她喊我，我都还没弄完。她说做菜的人在火候上偷懒，味道一定会把他揪出来。每个星期她会让我搅一次锅，告诉我该看什么。"},"course":{"tw":[["class",0],["round",3],["hunt",2],["long",6],["feed",0],["waste",3],["move",2],["beyond",6],["form",0]],"en":"I took a long course in woodwork one winter, and it was the best thing I ever did. There were twelve of us in the class, and the teacher would move from bench to bench and feed us advice in small amounts. In the first round he had us form a simple joint, and half of us made a waste of good timber. Beyond the window there was a field where he liked to hunt for old wood after a storm. It was the only course I ever finished. I still have the box I made in it, and the lid does not fit.","zh":"有一年冬天我上了一门很长的木工课，那是我做过最值的一件事。班上有十二个人，老师一个工作台一个工作台地走，一点一点给我们喂经验。头一轮他让我们做一个简单的榫接，我们一半人把好木料糟蹋了。窗外有块地，他一刮完风就爱去那儿捡旧木头。这是我唯一读完的一门课。我做的那只盒子还在，盖子合不上。"},"court":{"tw":[["romance",0],["chase",3],["act",2],["judge",6],["tribunal",0],["display",3],["room",2],["supreme",6],["courtyard",0]],"en":"The court sat in a small room at the back of the building, with a courtyard where the cars were parked. The judge came in, and everyone had to stand. It was not a supreme tribunal; it was a local matter about a fence. The two families had been in a long romance with the law, and each of them would display every paper they had ever signed. The younger son would chase the older one round the yard before the hearing began. It was hard to believe that any of it was meant to act as justice.","zh":"法庭设在楼后一间小屋里，外头是个停车的院子。法官进来，所有人都得站起来。这不是什么最高法院，只是为一堵篱笆闹的本地小事。这两家人跟法律纠缠了好些年，各自都愿意把签过的每一张纸摊出来。正式开庭前，小儿子还绕着院子追大儿子。很难相信这中间有哪一样是为了主持公道。"},"cover":{"tw":[["address",0],["coat",3],["dress",2],["short",6],["back",0],["course",3],["fire",2],["full",6],["continue",0]],"en":"The cover of the old book had come away at the back, and the address of a bookshop was written inside it in pencil. My mother would dress the torn corner with a piece of cloth, and then put a coat of thin glue along the spine. It took a short time to do, but it had to be done again every year. Of course she could not continue like that for ever. One winter evening, when the fire was full and the house was warm, she read the whole book aloud to me instead.","zh":"那本旧书的封面在书脊那边脱开了，里面用铅笔写着一家书店的地址。我妈会用一块布把撕破的角贴好，再沿着书脊抹一层薄胶。这花不了多少工夫，可每年都得再来一遍。她当然不能一直这样下去。有一个冬天的晚上，炉火正旺、屋里正暖，她索性把整本书念给我听了。"},"cross":{"tw":[["cover",2],["course",3],["meet",2],["along",6],["mark",0],["drive",3],["pass",2],["through",6],["track",0]],"en":"There is a stone cross at the place where two tracks meet, and you have to drive past it to reach the farm. We would walk along the field edge and then cross the stream at the old course. My father would mark the spot with a stick so we could find it again in the dark. As we came through the gate the rain began, and he put a cover over his head. It was a long pass of bad weather, and we were glad to see the light of the house.","zh":"两条小路交汇的地方立着一座石十字，开车去农场得从它旁边过。我们会沿着田边走过去，再从老河道那儿蹚过溪。我爸用一根树枝在那儿做个记号，好让我们黑天也能再找到。我们穿进大门的时候下起了雨，他把一块布顶在头上。这一阵坏天气拖得很久，远远看见屋里的灯，我们都松了口气。"},"cut":{"tw":[["burn",0],["check",3],["change",2],["drop",6],["issue",0],["kill",3],["free",2],["over",6],["track",0]],"en":"The cut on my hand was small but deep, and it would not stop bleeding. My mother had to check it twice, then change the cloth and hold it down hard. She said the cold could kill the feeling in my fingers, so she kept the fire going all night and would not let it burn out. In the morning the doctor had to cut the thread and set me free. No sport for a week, he said, and dropped the needle in the tray. I went back to the track the next day anyway, over the field behind the house. The issue never came up again.","zh":"我手上那道口子不大，可很深，血止不住。我妈核了两遍，换过布，又使劲按住。她说受凉会让手指头没了知觉，所以整夜守着炉子，不让火灭下去。早上去拆线，医生把线剪开，我就自由了。他说：一个星期不许运动，顺手把针丢进盘子里。第二天我照旧上了那条跑道，从屋后的田里绕过去。这事后来再没人提起。"},"deal":{"tw":[["address",0],["market",3],["act",2],["bid",6],["care",0],["meet",3],["board",2],["plan",6],["cover",0]],"en":"The deal was made in the market on a Saturday, with no paper and no witness. My father would meet the man at the board by the gate, shake hands, and then act as if nothing had happened. He had to bid low at first, because he did not care to look eager. His plan was always the same: wait until the other man was tired, then cover the last offer and walk away. I once asked him for the address of the buyer, and he said he had never needed one.","zh":"这桩买卖是星期六在集市上谈成的，没有纸，也没有证人。我爸会在门边那块木板旁跟人碰头，握个手，然后装作什么都没发生。开头他得压低价，因为他不乐意显出着急的样子。他那套打算从来不变：等对方累了，再把最后那个价码补上，然后走人。有一回我问他买主的地址，他说他从来用不着。"},"dig":{"tw":[["labour",0],["drive",3],["touch",2],["hole",6],["grasp",0],["figure",3],["understand",2],["mud",6],["excavate",0]],"en":"We had to dig a hole for the new tree, and the ground was hard as stone. My grandfather did the labour himself, though he could hardly grasp the handle by the end. He would drive the spade down with his foot, touch the mud at the bottom to see how wet it was, and then go on. He said I should figure out where the roots would go before I started. It took me years to understand what he meant. When they came to excavate the old bed years later, the tree was still standing.","zh":"我们得给新树挖个坑，那土硬得像石头。活是我爷爷自己干的，到后来他几乎握不住锹把。他用脚把铲子蹬下去，摸摸坑底的泥看湿不湿，然后接着挖。他说动手之前我该先琢磨清楚根会往哪儿伸。等我明白他的意思，已经过去好几年了。多年后有人来挖那口旧花坛时，那棵树还站着。"},"dirty":{"tw":[["soil",0],["pollute",3],["change",2],["clean",1],["stuff",6],["foul",3],["splash",3],["trash",6],["grime",0]],"en":"The dog came in dirty from the yard, and there was grime on every step he crossed. He had rolled in something foul and then splashed through the puddle by the gate. My father had to change the cloth on the floor and take the whole thing out to the trash. He said the soil near the road had been polluted for years, and that nothing but weeds would grow there. Do not let him bring that stuff inside, my mother said. I had to give him a bath before he could come in. He was a different animal once he was clean, and he knew it.","zh":"狗从院子里进来，脏得不行，它踏过的每一级台阶上都留下污印。它先在一摊臭东西上滚过，又从门边的水坑里扑腾过来。我爸只好换掉地上的布，把脏东西全都扔到垃圾堆去。他说路边那块土被污染好些年了，除了野草什么都长不出来。我妈说：别让它把那些玩意儿带进屋。我只好先给它洗个澡才让它进来。干净以后它就成了另一只狗，它自己也知道。"},"discover":{"tw":[["break",0],["blow",3],["tell",2],["how",6],["find",2],["see",3],["spy",2],["locate",6],["hear",0]],"en":"I had to discover where the noise was coming from, and I did not know how to start. I could hear it in every room but could not locate it. Then the wind gave a great blow and the door began to break loose in its frame. I went out to see what it was, and I had to tell my mother at once. There was a small pipe under the step, and when I put my hand on it I could find the leak. My neighbour had once worked as a spy, and he said he would have taken half an hour to do the same.","zh":"我得弄清楚这声音是从哪儿来的，可我不知道该从哪儿下手。每个屋里都听得见，就是找不着它在哪。后来一阵大风刮过，那扇门在框子里松开了。我出去看是怎么回事，得马上告诉我妈。台阶底下有根细管子，我手一放上去就摸到了漏的地方。我邻居从前干过谍报，他说同样的事他得花半小时。"},"dog":{"tw":[["tail",0],["tree",3],["catch",2],["cat",6],["track",0],["quest",3],["support",2],["horse",6],["chase",0]],"en":"The old dog could not chase anything now, but he still liked to follow a track along the field. He would put his nose down at the tree by the gate and go on for an hour. Once he caught a cat in the yard and never heard the end of it. He had been a support to my father in the years when there was little else. My grandfather kept a horse in those days, and the two animals were a strange pair, with the dog wagging his tail at the stable door. His last quest was for a bone he had buried himself.","zh":"那条老狗现在什么也追不上了，可它还是喜欢顺着田边跟一条踪迹走。它会在大门旁那棵树底下把鼻子贴到地上，一跟就是一个钟头。有一回它在院子里逮住了一只猫，从此这事被念叨个没完。在那些什么都没有的年头，它是我爸的一个依靠。我爷爷那时候养着一匹马，这两只牲口是奇怪的一对儿，狗总在棚门口摇着尾巴。它最后一次找东西，是找自己埋起来的一根骨头。"},"drink":{"tw":[["swallow",0],["carry",3],["use",2],["beer",6],["toast",0],["milk",3],["consume",2],["juice",6],["pledge",0]],"en":"After the long walk the old man stopped at the well and had a drink of cold water. He would not swallow it fast, though the day was hot and his shirt was wet. He had carried a small tin cup for years, and he used it now, the way his father had. On the table by the door stood a bottle of beer, a glass of milk and some juice for the children, because young bodies consume more than his does. At dinner his son raised a toast to him and said a few quiet words. Then they all made a pledge to walk that road again next spring.","zh":"走了大半天的路，老人在井边停下，喝了一大口凉水。天热，衬衫都湿透了，可他喝得并不急。那只小铁杯他带了很多年，这回还是用它，跟他父亲当年一样。门边的桌上摆着一瓶啤酒、一杯牛奶，还有给孩子们准备的果汁，年轻人的身子总比他耗得多。晚饭时儿子向他举杯，说了几句轻的话。然后一家人立了个约：明年春天再走那条路。"},"drop":{"tw":[["fall",0],["blow",3],["change",2],["rise",6],["miss",0],["forget",3],["drug",2],["price",6],["spend",0]],"en":"When the price of the drug dropped at the chemist on the corner, the whole street felt the change. The old woman did not want to miss it. She had to spend most of her money on it every month, and she could not forget the winter when the cost began to rise. A cold wind began to blow along the pavement, and a leaf started to fall past the window. She watched one single drop of rain slide down the glass and stop. In her hand the small box was light, almost nothing. She put it in her bag and walked home slowly.","zh":"街角药铺里那种药一降价，整条街都感觉到了变化。老太太不想错过。她每个月都得把大部分钱花在这上面，也忘不了药价开始往上涨的那个冬天。冷风沿着人行道吹，一片黄叶开始从窗前落下。她看着一滴雨顺着玻璃往下滑，停住了。手里那只小盒子轻得几乎没分量。她把它放进包里，慢慢走回家。"},"church":{"tw":[["ecclesiastic",4],["cathedral",3],["body",2],["catholic",6],["basilica",3],["service",2],["chapel",6]],"en":"The old church stood at the top of the hill, and beyond it you could see the towers of the cathedral. On Sunday the whole village came up for the service. An ecclesiastic in a plain robe read the names of the dead from a book. Beside him a small chapel held candles for those who could not come. People of every kind, catholic or not, stood together in the cold. Even the basilica further down the road could not hold a crowd like this. The body of the building was cold, but the singing was warm. Nobody spoke above a whisper.","zh":"那座老教堂立在山冈顶上，越过它就能看见大教堂的塔楼。礼拜天，全村的人都上来做礼拜。一位穿素袍的教士照着书念亡者的名字。他旁边一间小礼拜堂里点着蜡烛，给来不了的人留着。无论是不是天主教徒，各种各样的人都在冷风里站在一起。就连路那头的大教堂也装不下这样一群人。这栋建筑的主体是冷的，歌声却是暖的。没有人大声说话。"},"accept":{"tw":[["admit",0],["agree",3],["refuse",1],["seek",6],["bear",0],["believe",3],["negotiate",6],["assume",0]],"en":"When the manager offered me the job, I did not accept it at once. I asked for a day to think, because I could not bear to decide too fast. He did not refuse me; he only said he would wait. I had to negotiate a small point about the hours, and he agreed in the end. He told me to seek advice from anyone I trusted. I began to assume I would take it, though I did not admit this even to myself. It was a quiet office, and the pay was fair. I still do not believe I made a mistake.","zh":"经理把这份工作给我时，我没有马上答应。我请他给我一天想想，因为我实在不敢决定得太快。他没有拒绝，只说会等。工时上有一小点我得谈，最后他同意了。他让我去找信得过的人商量。我开始设想自己会接下它，虽然连对自己也没承认。那是一间安静的办公室，待遇也公道。到现在我仍不觉得这是个错。"},"age":{"tw":[["mature",0],["reign",3],["change",2],["rejuvenate",1],["life",6],["antiquity",3],["develop",2],["same",6]],"en":"At his age my grandfather had seen the whole town change. His life had begun in a time of antiquity, he liked to say, and he had watched the young grow up and leave. A king had once had his reign in those years, though that was before I was born. My grandfather was slow to mature, my mother joked, and never the same for two days. He had also watched the town develop new roads and new houses. To rejuvenate himself he would walk to the river every morning and sit in the sun. He said a long age teaches you patience.","zh":"在我爷爷这把年纪，他眼看着整个镇子变了样。他总爱说，他的一生开始得很早很早，那时还是古旧的年月，他看着年轻人长大、离开。那些年里曾有位国王在位，不过那是我出生前的事了。我妈打趣说，他这个人成熟得慢，两天一个样。他也看着镇子修起新路、盖起新房子。为了让自己恢复点精神，他每天早上都走到河边，坐在太阳底下。他说活得久，能教会你耐心。"},"amount":{"tw":[["total",0],["figure",3],["magnitude",2],["excess",6],["measure",0],["advance",3],["value",6],["quantity",0]],"en":"The total on the bill was larger than I had expected. I had to measure each item again and write down the figure, because the amount of paper alone surprised me. The quantity of ink we had used was small, but the value of the work was high. There was an excess of charges I did not understand. The shop asked for an advance before they would begin. I read it twice and still could not believe it. Only then did I see the magnitude of the job I had taken on. In the end I paid and said nothing.","zh":"账单上的总数比我预想的多。我只好把每样东西又量了一遍，把数目写下来，因为光是纸张的量就让我吃了一惊。我们用的墨并不多，可这活儿的价值不低。里面有些收费我根本看不懂，多出来一大截。店家要求先付一笔预付款才肯开工。我读了两遍，还是不敢相信。到这时我才看清自己接下的是多大一件事。最后我付了钱，什么也没说。"},"back":{"tw":[["cover",0],["tail",3],["bet",2],["ahead",1],["game",0],["champion",3],["lie",2],["second",0]],"en":"At the race I put a small bet on a horse I had never seen. The champion from last year was ahead of the others from the start, but my horse stayed near the back of the pack. Its tail was the last thing I could see as they came round. For a second I thought I had lost my money. Then the leader began to tire, and mine moved up. I lay my ticket on the bench and waited. The race was a long game, and the cover of the stands kept off the rain.","zh":"赛场上，我在一匹从没见过的马上下了一小注。去年的冠军一开跑就冲在前面，我那匹马却一直待在队伍后头。等它们转过弯来，我只能看见它的尾巴。有那么一秒，我以为钱没了。接着领先的马开始没劲，我的那匹往上赶。我把票放在长凳上等着。这是一场漫长的较量，看台的顶棚挡住了雨。"},"bad":{"tw":[["big",0],["worse",3],["quality",2],["good",1],["little",6],["tough",0],["evil",3],["bit",6]],"en":"The storm that week was bad, and the roof began to leak in the big room. My father said the quality of the old tiles was poor, and the rain would only make things worse. There was a little water in a dish on the floor. He had a tough job ahead, up on the roof in the wind. He did not believe in evil luck, only in good work. He took off his coat, climbed up, and fixed a bit of the edge before dark. By morning the leak had stopped, but the wall was stained. We would have to paint it in spring.","zh":"那一周的暴风雨来得很凶，大房间的屋顶开始漏。我爸说这些旧瓦质量差，雨一下只会更糟。地板上一个盘子里接了一小点水。他眼前是桩难办的活儿，得顶着风爬到屋顶上去。他不信什么厄运，只信好好干活。他脱了外套爬上去，天黑前把边上一小块修好了。到早上漏水是停了，可墙上留了痕。等春天还得重新刷一遍。"},"bag":{"tw":[["base",0],["pouch",3],["pack",2],["plastic",6],["dish",0],["steal",2],["bottle",6],["pocket",0]],"en":"My mother packed a bag for the picnic and put it on the base of the cart. Inside were a plastic dish, a bottle of water, and a small pouch of salt. She told me to pack the fruit on top so it would not get crushed. On the way a boy tried to steal the bag from the cart, but he only reached the pocket and ran off. My father laughed and said nothing had been taken. We spread a cloth and sat down on the grass. We ate by the river and were home before dark. It was a good day after all.","zh":"我妈为野餐装了一个袋子，放在推车的最下面。里面有一个塑料盘、一瓶水，还有一小袋盐。她让我把水果放在最上面，免得压坏。路上有个男孩想从车上偷走袋子，可他只够到口袋就跑了。我爸笑了，说什么也没丢。我们摊开布，坐在草地上。我们在河边吃了饭，天黑前就到家了。那一天到头来还挺好。"},"bird":{"tw":[["skirt",0],["parrot",3],["cry",2],["shark",6],["hiss",0],["observe",2],["whale",6],["shuttle",0]],"en":"In the garden a bright bird sat on the fence and would not move. It looked like a small parrot, and when my sister came near, it gave a sharp cry and a low hiss. I stood still and began to observe it. Its long tail feathers hung down over the wood like a skirt. That morning the news had shown a whale and a shark in the same bay, and now this little thing seemed just as strange. Then a shuttle bus passed, and the bird flew off. I have never seen one like it since.","zh":"园子里有只颜色鲜亮的鸟停在篱笆上，不肯动。它看着像只小鹦鹉，我妹妹一靠近，它就尖声一叫，还低低地嘶了一声。我站住不动，开始仔细看它。它长长的尾羽像条裙子，垂在木头上。那天早上的新闻里，同一片海湾出现了鲸和鲨鱼，如今这小东西看着也一样稀奇。一辆班车开过，鸟就飞走了。从那以后我再没见过那样的鸟。"},"birth":{"tw":[["bear",0],["drop",3],["produce",2],["death",1],["child",6],["nativity",0],["twin",3],["maternal",6]],"en":"On the farm we waited all night for the birth of the first lamb. The old ewe had to bear it alone, and we could only watch from the door. Just before dawn she began to produce a second one: twins. My aunt, whose maternal care never failed, wrapped them both in cloth to keep them warm. My youngest cousin, still a child, held one in her arms. A single drop of blood on the straw told us all was well. That night there had been no thought of death, only of new life. I still remember the small nativity in the barn.","zh":"在农场上，我们为第一只羊羔的出生守了一整夜。老母羊只能自己生，我们只能站在门边看。天快亮时，她又生出一只：一对双胞胎。我姑姑那份母性的照料从不含糊，用布把两只都裹起来保暖。我最小的表妹还是个孩子，把一只抱在怀里。草上的一滴血告诉我们一切顺利。那一晚没人想到死，只想到新生命。我至今还记得谷仓里那一幕小小的降生。"},"bit":{"tw":[["act",0],["chew",3],["taste",2],["pretty",6],["chip",0],["scale",3],["little",6],["minute",0]],"en":"I broke off a bit of chocolate and let it melt on my tongue. It had a pretty sweet taste, and I began to chew the little pieces slowly. My sister said it was a common act of greed, and she was right. I measured a chip of it on the kitchen scale, just to see, and the number was tiny. It took only a minute to eat the lot. It was a small pleasure on a slow afternoon. I did not tell anyone about it. Then I had to wash the dish and start again with what was left.","zh":"我掰下一小块巧克力，让它在舌头上化开。味道甜得很讨喜，我开始慢慢嚼那些小碎块。我妹妹说这是典型的贪嘴，她说得没错。我还拿厨房的秤称了一小片，就想看看，数字小得可怜。吃光它只用了一分钟。这是慢悠悠的下午里一点小小的享受。这事我谁也没告诉。然后我只好洗碗，再拿剩下的重来一遍。"},"blood":{"tw":[["line",0],["family",3],["genealogy",2],["heart",6],["rip",0],["side",3],["stomach",6],["stock",0]],"en":"The doctor took a little blood from my arm to check my heart. He said my family had a long line of strong people on my mother's side. My grandfather had once drawn up a whole genealogy of our stock, tracing every branch back for years. I had a small rip in my coat, and I held my stomach while I waited, more nervous than I wanted to admit. An old woman in the next chair told me not to worry. When the result came, the doctor only smiled. She said we are all the same inside. There was nothing wrong with me.","zh":"医生从我胳膊上取了一点血，检查我的心脏。他说我母亲这一支，家里世世代代都是硬朗的人。我爷爷曾把我们家这一脉的家谱整理得清清楚楚，往上追了好多年，每一支都不落。我外套上有个小口子，等着的时候我捂着肚子，比嘴上承认的要紧张。旁边椅子上的老太太叫我别担心。结果出来时，医生只是笑笑。她说，人里头其实都一样。我什么毛病都没有。"},"body":{"tw":[["trunk",0],["church",3],["system",2],["blood",6],["personify",0],["public",3],["message",2],["hand",6]],"en":"The old statue in front of the church showed a whole body carved from one piece of stone. Its trunk was plain, and one hand was missing. Someone had tried to personify the town itself in that figure, as if the place could stand and look at us. Inside, the museum had a small system of rooms, each with its own message. There was a picture of a heart and the blood inside it. A guide said it had belonged to the public for two hundred years. People walked past it without a second look. It had stood there for a long time.","zh":"教堂前的旧雕像是一整个人体，由一整块石头刻成。它的躯干平平的，一只手缺了。有人想把这座小镇本身拟人化在那个人像里，好像这地方能站起来看着我们。里面，博物馆是一小套房间连成的，每间都有自己的话要说。有一张图画的是一颗心，还有里面流动的血。向导说，它两百年来一直属于公众。人们从它旁边走过，连头都不回。它在那儿站了很久很久。"},"business":{"tw":[["job",0],["position",3],["commerce",2],["industry",6],["line",0],["career",3],["corporate",6],["occupation",0]],"en":"My aunt ran a small business in the market, and she had done so all her working life. Her job began before light, when she would open the shutters and arrange the goods. In her line of trade, commerce was simple: buy cheap, sell fair, and know your customers. She had never wanted a corporate position or a big career. She said a good occupation was one you did not dread in the morning. The local industry grew around shops like hers. She knew every face that came through the door. And she never once thought of leaving it.","zh":"我姑姑在市场里经营一家小店，一辈子的营生都在那儿。天不亮她就开工，拉起卷帘门，摆好货。在她这一行里，买卖的道理很简单：进得便宜，卖得公道，认得熟客。她从没想过进什么大公司，也没想过飞黄腾达。她说，好职业就是早上不会让你害怕去上的那种。当地的产业就是围着这样的小店发展起来的。从门口进来的每张脸她都认得。她也从没想过要离开。"},"buy":{"tw":[["steal",0],["subscribe",3],["pay",2],["sell",1],["offer",6],["purchase",0],["cash",6],["bargain",0]],"en":"At the market my father wanted to buy a new coat, but first he had to sell the old one. The seller would not offer a good price, so they began to bargain. In the end he agreed to pay in cash. It was his first purchase of the year, and it made him happy. He told me never to steal, but to save and buy things honestly. I asked him if we could subscribe to a magazine as well, and he said maybe next month. The coat was warm and dark and fitted him well. I still have it today.","zh":"在集市上，我爸想买一件新外套，可先得把旧的卖掉。卖家不肯出好价，两人就开始讲价。最后他同意付现金。这是他今年头一笔购置，他很高兴。他告诉我千万别偷东西，要攒钱，光明正大地买。我问他能不能顺便订一本杂志，他说下个月再说。那件外套又暖又深色，穿在他身上正合适。到今天我还留着它。"},"camp":{"tw":[["pack",0],["loop",3],["change",2],["where",6],["tent",0],["pitch",2],["fire",6],["encamp",0]],"en":"We left home early to camp by the lake. Where the road ended, we had to pack everything into our bags and walk the last mile. We chose a flat place and began to pitch the tent. A loop of rope held the front open. Then my father started a small fire to cook on. We could not change the weather, but the night was still and warm. A family had encamped near us, and their voices carried over the water until late. I slept badly, but I did not mind. In the morning the lake was as flat as glass.","zh":"我们一早出门，去湖边露营。路到头的地方，我们只好把东西都装进包里，走完最后一段。我们挑了一块平地，开始支帐篷。一根绳圈把前面撑开。然后我爸生了小火做饭。天气我们改不了，好在这一夜又静又暖。有一家人也在我们旁边扎了营，他们的说话声越过水面，一直到很晚。我睡得不好，可我不在乎。早上湖面平得像玻璃。"},"centre":{"tw":[["eye",0],["listen",3],["move",2],["main",6],["heart",0],["seat",3],["international",6],["middle",0]],"en":"We met in the centre of town, by the main square, and walked to the concert hall together. My seat was near the middle of the row, close to the stage. I could not take my eye off the singer, who stood right at the heart of the light. Her voice seemed to move through the whole room and hold every listener still. There was an international group in the front row who had come a long way to hear her. All I could do was listen. When it ended, nobody moved for a moment. Then everyone stood up and clapped.","zh":"我们在市中心那家大广场碰面，一起走到音乐厅。我的座位在那一排的中间，离舞台很近。我的眼睛离不开那位歌手，她就站在光的最里头。她的声音好像穿过整个大厅，把每个听的人都定住了。前排有一群从很远地方赶来的外国听众。我能做的只有听。一曲终了，好一会儿没人动。然后所有人都站起来鼓掌。"},"club":{"tw":[["order",0],["hunt",3],["hit",2],["league",6],["lodge",0],["wood",3],["meet",2],["team",6]],"en":"Our club met every Thursday in a small lodge at the edge of the wood. There was a league in the county, and our team was not the best, but we played hard. The coach would order us to run until the light went, and then we would hunt for the ball in the long grass. I could hit it further than anyone, but my hands were always cold. Afterwards we would sit by the fire and talk about the next match. The wood gave us sticks for the winter fire. It was the best part of my week.","zh":"我们俱乐部每周四在林边一间小屋里碰头。县里有个联赛，我们队不是最强的，但踢得很拼。教练会命令我们跑到天黑，然后我们就在深草里找球。我踢得比谁都远，可手总是凉的。结束后我们会坐在火边，聊下一场比赛。林子给我们捡来冬天烧火的柴。那是我一周里最好的时光。"},"coat":{"tw":[["cake",0],["egg",3],["cover",2],["scarf",6],["surface",0],["fur",3],["dress",2],["yellow",6]],"en":"On a cold morning my mother put on her heavy coat and a wool scarf. She was going to make a cake for the village fair. The surface of the table was covered with flour. She broke an egg into the bowl and began to mix. A yellow dress hung on the back of the door, waiting for the fair. Beside it lay a fur hat she never wore. The kitchen smelled of sugar and warm milk. She told me to cover the cake and keep it warm, and not to touch it until the evening. It was the best cake she ever made.","zh":"一个冷早上，我妈穿上厚外套，围上羊毛围巾。她要做个蛋糕，送去村里的集市。桌面上一层薄薄的粉。她往碗里磕了个鸡蛋，开始搅。门背后挂着一条黄裙子，等着集市那天穿。旁边放着一顶毛皮帽子，她从来不戴。厨房里满是糖和温牛奶的味道。她叫我把蛋糕盖好保温，不到晚上别去碰。那是她做过最好吃的蛋糕。"},"collect":{"tw":[["gather",0],["catch",3],["store",2],["obtain",6],["compile",0],["farm",3],["check",6],["cod",0]],"en":"Every autumn we would collect apples from the old trees on the farm. My grandfather would gather them into baskets and store the best ones in the shed. It was hard to obtain good fruit in a wet year, he said, and you had to check each one. He had tried to compile a list of the trees, with their names and ages. Once he caught a boy taking apples without asking, but he only laughed and gave him a bag. Later, at the market, he sold dried cod beside the fruit.","zh":"每年秋天，我们都会到农场上那几棵老树去收苹果。我爷爷把苹果收进筐里，把最好的存在棚屋中。他说，雨水多的年份很难得到好果子，每一个都得查过。他曾想给这些树编一份名单，写上名字和年龄。有一回他撞见一个男孩不问自取地摘苹果，可他只是笑笑，还给了他一个袋子。后来在市场，他在水果旁边卖起了干鳕鱼。"},"cool":{"tw":[["chill",0],["ice",3],["change",2],["heat",1],["hot",6],["poise",0],["quench",3],["bit",6]],"en":"After a long walk in the heat, I wanted something cool to drink. I put a little ice in a glass and watched it change into water. The first sip seemed to quench a thirst I had carried all day. A small wind moved through the garden. My father kept his poise even in the hottest weather; he would not rush and would not complain. He said the summer chill of the evening was the best part of the day. I drank the last bit and lay back in the shade. I closed my eyes and let it pass over me.","zh":"在热天里走了很久，我只想喝点凉的。我在杯子里放了几块冰，看着它化成水。第一口好像把我一整天的渴都浇下去了。一阵小风穿过园子。再热的天，我爸也沉得住气，不慌也不抱怨。他说傍晚那点凉意是一天里最好的时候。我喝掉最后一点，靠回阴凉里。我闭上眼，任它拂过我身上。"},"cost":{"tw":[["price",3],["charge",3],["value",2],["pay",6],["toll",0],["expense",3],["necessitate",2],["increase",6]],"en":"The repair came at a higher cost than we had planned. The mechanic gave me the price on paper, and I had to pay it before I could take the car. There was an extra charge for the parts, and the toll on the road home would add a little more. My father said the real value of the work was not in the money. Still, the expense would increase our troubles that month, and would necessitate some small cuts at home. In the end the car ran as well as new. That was worth more than the sum we paid.","zh":"这次修车的花费比我们计划的高。修理工把价钱写在纸上给我，我得先付钱才能把车开走。零件还另外收了费，回家路上的过路费又要多添一点。我爸说，这活儿真正的价值不在钱上。可这笔开销还是会让我们那个月更紧张，家里也得省下一些。最后车开起来跟新的一样。这比我们付的那笔钱值多了。"},"couple":{"tw":[["pair",2],["ride",3],["family",2],["husband",6],["match",0],["serve",3],["join",2],["mate",0]],"en":"My sister and her husband were a quiet couple who ran a small guesthouse by the sea. Every guest got the same welcome: a warm meal served at a long table, where strangers would join them and talk like old mates. In summer the two of them would ride an old bike down to the market, a pair of baskets on the back. People said they were a perfect match. Their whole family came once a year, and on those nights she would serve soup until the pot was empty. Nothing there was ever hurried, and few guests wanted to leave.","zh":"我姐姐和她丈夫是一对安静的人，在海边开了家小客栈。每位客人受到的招待都一样：长桌上热腾腾的饭，陌生人坐下来跟他们一起吃，聊得像老相识。夏天两人会骑一辆旧自行车去集市，后座挂着两只篮子。人人都说他们是天生的一对。每年全家来一次，那些晚上她会一直盛汤，直到锅底见空。那屋里什么都不着急，走的时候也少有人舍得。"},"double":{"tw":[["image",0],["hit",2],["single",1],["triple",6],["repeat",0],["raise",2],["straight",6],["dual",0]],"en":"A man in the print shop had to make a double copy of every photograph, because the image on the first sheet often came out grey. He would raise the whole plate and press it down straight, then repeat the move until the lines were clean. A single mistake could ruin a run of a hundred. When a job was late he would hit the old machine with his hand, and it would start again. Some machines were dual, with two rolls; the best ones could print a triple set at once. He never threw away a bad sheet.","zh":"印刷铺里的一个人得把每张照片都印成双份，因为第一张纸上的影像常常发灰。他会把整块印版抬起来，笔直地按下去，再重复这个动作，直到线条干净。出一次错就能毁掉一百张。活儿赶得紧时他会用手拍一下旧机器，它就又转起来了。有些机器是双滚筒的，最好的一台一次能印三份。他从不扔掉一张印坏的纸。"},"down":{"tw":[["blue",0],["submarine",3],["better",2],["back",6],["kill",0],["doctor",2],["close",6],["land",0]],"en":"From the top of the cliff the path went straight down to a small beach, and the water there was a deep blue. My uncle had been a doctor on a submarine before he came back to live with us. He said you learn to close your eyes and sleep when the boat goes down, because the land is far and the sea is not gentle. Twice he had to help kill a fire in the engine room. He told the story better each year. The worst night, he said, was when they had to bring a sick man back up and land him before morning.","zh":"从崖顶有条小路直通下面一片小沙滩，那儿的海水是深蓝色的。我叔在回到我们身边之前，曾在一艘潜艇上当过医生。他说船一下潜，你就得学会闭眼睡觉，因为陆地在很远的地方，海又不温柔。有两次他得帮忙扑灭机舱里的火。这故事他一年比一年讲得好。他说最难的那一夜，是他们把一个病人送上水面，赶在天亮前送上了岸。"},"advertise":{"tw":[["push",0],["bill",3],["announce",2],["merchandise",6],["plug",3],["praise",2],["sell",6]],"en":"To advertise the new shop, my cousin would push flyers through every door in the street. He would announce a free gift for the first customer and praise his own goods in a loud voice. The bill for the printing was more than he had planned. He would plug the shop on the local radio, badly, and people loved it. A pile of merchandise sat in the window for a week. In the end it worked, and he sold more in one month than in the year before. He was proud of himself for a long time.","zh":"为了给新店做宣传，我表哥把传单塞进街上每一户的门缝。他会宣布第一位客人有赠品，再扯着嗓子夸自家的货。印刷的账单比他想的多。他在本地电台给店里做广告，说得磕磕巴巴，大家反倒爱听。一堆货物在橱窗里摆了一个星期。到头来还真管用，他一个月的销量比前一年一整年还多。他为此得意了好久。"},"animal":{"tw":[["creature",0],["giant",3],["organism",2],["insect",6],["beast",0],["larva",3],["fauna",0]],"en":"At the pond my father would show me every small creature he could find. Under a stone there was often a larva, and once we saw a giant insect with shining wings. He said every organism in that water had its own work to do. He would name the fauna of the valley like old friends, from the smallest beetle to the beast that left tracks in the mud. Once a fox came to the edge and drank, a wild animal in the open. I learned to sit still and watch.","zh":"在池塘边，我爸会把他能找到的每一种小生物指给我看。石头底下常常有条幼虫，有一次我们还看见一只长着亮翅膀的大虫子。他说那片水里的每个生命都有自己的事要做。他会像念老朋友的名字一样数出山谷里的各种动物，从最小的甲虫到在泥里留下脚印的野兽。有一次一只狐狸走到水边喝水，一只野生的动物就那么坦然地露着面。我学会了坐着不动地看。"},"area":{"tw":[["country",0],["corner",3],["environment",2],["field",0],["front",3],["extent",2],["region",2]],"en":"After the storm, the whole area looked different. In one front corner of the field, the wind had torn down a line of young trees, and the damage reached across the region. My father stood at the edge and tried to judge the extent of it. He said the country had not seen such weather in years, and that the environment would take a long time to recover. We walked the wet ground slowly, side by side. Even the far side of the valley, past the low stone wall, was quiet and broken.","zh":"风暴过后，整个地区都变了样。田里靠前的一角，风把一排小树刮倒了，破坏一直延伸到整个区域。我父亲站在边上，想估量一下范围有多大。他说这地方多年没见过这种天气，环境要很久才能恢复。我们并排慢慢走过那片湿地。就连山谷那一头、矮石墙那边，也安静而残破。"},"begin":{"tw":[["start",3],["act",2],["end",1],["resume",6],["commence",0],["talk",2],["next",6]],"en":"At nine the meeting would begin, and nobody was ready. The manager took a breath, said we would commence with the short report, and then he began to talk about the numbers. He stopped in the middle, waited, and told us the work would start again next week. There was an act at the fair that evening, and he wanted to end the day there. When the break was over, he asked us to resume. I wrote everything down and stayed until the room was empty. On the way out, a woman asked me what had been decided. I said I did not know, and that was the truth.","zh":"会议九点开始，可谁都没准备好。经理吸了口气，说我们先从那份简短报告讲起，然后他就开始谈那些数字。他中途停下，等了一会儿，告诉我们工作下周重新开始。那天晚上集市上有个节目，他想在那里结束一天。休息结束后，他让大家接着来。我把一切都记下来，一直待到屋里空了。出去时有个女人问我决定了什么。我说我不知道，而这是实话。"},"best":{"tw":[["better",0],["beat",2],["good",6],["scoop",0],["attempt",2],["play",6],["trump",0]],"en":"We played cards on Sunday, and my sister had the best hand of the night. She had a good eye for the game and would not beat about the bush. Every attempt to trump her failed, one after another. The better player always wins, she said, and she took the whole scoop of coins. It was only a small play, but she loved it. I made one last attempt, lost again, and laughed with the rest. She kept her coins in a little tin box and counted them twice before she left. My father watched from the door and said nothing.","zh":"星期天我们打牌，我妹妹摸到了那晚最好的一手牌。她打牌眼很毒，从不绕弯子。每一次想盖过她的尝试都失败了，一个接一个。她说，好手总是赢，然后把那一堆硬币全揽过去。不过是小打小闹，可她就爱这个。我又试了最后一次，还是输，跟着大家笑起来。她把硬币收在一只小铁盒里，走之前数了两遍。我父亲站在门口看着，什么也没说。"},"black":{"tw":[["dark",5],["man",2],["white",1],["blue",6],["dim",0],["red",6]],"en":"The old man wore a black coat all winter, even when the sun was out. In the dim light of the hall his back looked almost blue, and only the white of his collar showed. He had a red scarf that he never took off, and he kept it folded under his arm like something precious. When the room grew dark, he would sit by the window and watch the street. I once asked him why. He said black hides the years better than any other colour. He was the quietest man on our street.","zh":"那位老人整个冬天都穿一件黑外套，哪怕出太阳也穿。走廊里光线昏暗，他的背看上去几乎发蓝，只有白领子露出来。他有一条红围巾，从不摘下，总像宝贝似的叠好夹在腋下。屋里暗下来时，他就坐在窗边看街。我问过一次为什么。他说黑色比别的颜色更藏得住年岁。他是我们街上最安静的人。"},"blue":{"tw":[["dark",0],["sky",2],["red",6],["low",0],["dye",2],["black",6],["naughty",0]],"en":"We dyed cloth in the yard all afternoon. My aunt wanted a deep blue for the curtains, so she mixed the dye with water and waited. The sky above us was a pale blue at first, then grew dark before we were done. My little cousin was naughty and dipped his hands in the pot, and they came out red. He held them up like a prize. We laughed, but my aunt made him wash them with the black soap until the colour was low and faint. By evening the line of cloth dried in the wind, and the whole yard smelled of wet dye.","zh":"我们在院子里染了一下午的布。我姑妈想要一块深蓝色的窗帘，于是把染料和上水，等着。头顶的天起初是淡蓝的，没等我们忙完就暗了下来。我小表弟很顽皮，把手伸进染缸，拿出来是红的。他举着两手像得了奖。我们笑，可姑妈让他用黑肥皂洗，一直洗到颜色淡下去。到傍晚，绳上的布在风里晾干，满院子都是湿染料的气味。"},"bone":{"tw":[["drum",0],["study",2],["tooth",6],["pearl",0],["white",2],["skull",6],["ivory",0]],"en":"In the study at the back of the museum, my teacher showed us a single bone. It was white as a pearl and smooth as ivory, and she said it had once been part of a skull. We had to write down its shape and size. Someone had tied a small drum beside it, and the skin was tight. I thought of my own tooth and how a fall could break something like this. Nobody spoke. The room smelled of old wood and dust. I asked what it had been, and she said a young man, long ago.","zh":"博物馆后面的研究室里，老师给我们看了一根骨头。它白得像珍珠，光得像象牙，她说这曾经是头骨的一部分。我们得记下它的形状和大小。旁边有人系了面小鼓，鼓面绷得很紧。我想起自己的牙，还有一次摔倒会不会把这样的东西摔断。谁都没说话。屋里是旧木头和灰尘的气味。我问它原来属于谁，她说是一个年轻人，很久以前。"},"box":{"tw":[["corner",0],["flat",3],["blow",2],["piece",6],["chest",3],["hit",2],["spot",6]],"en":"The box sat in the corner of the attic, flat and grey with dust. My brother gave it a blow with his hand, and a piece of the lid came off at once. Inside was an old chest of letters tied with string. He did not hit it again, afraid of what else might break. On the lid was a small spot where someone had spilled ink years ago. We carried it down to the kitchen and opened it slowly. The first letter was from my grandmother, written before I was born.","zh":"那口箱子放在阁楼的角落里，扁扁的，蒙着一层灰。我哥用手一拍，一块箱盖立刻掉了下来。里面是一只旧木匣，装着用绳子捆好的信。他没敢再拍，怕还有别的会碎。箱盖上有个小斑点，是多年前有人溅上的墨。我们把它搬到厨房，慢慢打开。第一封信是我奶奶写的，写在我出生之前。"},"bread":{"tw":[["scratch",0],["cracker",3],["cover",2],["toast",6],["sugar",0],["butter",6],["loot",0]],"en":"From scratch, my grandmother made bread every Friday. She would cover the dough with a cloth and let it rise by the stove. At breakfast we had toast with butter and a little sugar, and my father would eat a cracker while he read. The house smelled warm all morning. She said the loaf was better than any loot, because you could not steal the smell of it. We ate it while it was still hot. In winter she would bake two and give one to the neighbours. Nobody ever asked her why she did it; they only said thank you at the door.","zh":"每个星期五，我奶奶都从头做起烤面包。她用布把面团盖上，放在炉子边发起来。早饭我们吃抹黄油、撒一点糖的吐司，我父亲一边看报一边啃块脆饼。整个上午屋里都是暖香。她说这面包比任何抢来的东西都好，因为那股香味你偷不走。我们趁热吃。冬天她会烤两个，送一个给邻居。没人问过她为什么这么做，只在门口道声谢。"},"card":{"tw":[["bill",2],["paper",2],["check",6],["board",0],["record",2],["file",6],["notice",0]],"en":"At the front desk a young clerk pulled a card from the file and read it twice. On the board behind her hung a notice about new prices. She checked the bill, wrote the number on a sheet of paper, and put the card back. The record showed that the account had been open for years. I waited while she looked for one more file. Then she looked up and told me everything was in order. I paid in cash and asked her to keep the receipt. She smiled and said the office would send the rest by post.","zh":"前台一位年轻职员从档案里抽出一张卡片，读了两遍。她身后的板子上挂着一张新价目告示。她核了账单，把数字写在一张纸上，又把卡片放回去。记录显示这个账户开了好多年。我等着她再找一份档案。然后她抬起头，说一切都没问题。我付了现金，请她留好收据。她笑笑，说剩下的办公室会寄给我。"},"chair":{"tw":[["lead",0],["head",2],["floor",6],["president",0],["position",2],["board",6],["chairman",0]],"en":"The chairman of the board took his chair at the head of the table and asked us to sit. He had held the position for ten years and was said to lead without raising his voice. The president of the club sat beside him, hands flat on the floor of the old stage. Nobody moved. A young man with a folder stood at the back. When the chairman spoke, the whole room turned toward him. For an hour we argued about the budget, and then he closed the meeting with a single sentence.","zh":"董事会主席在长桌首端拉开椅子，请我们坐下。他这个位子坐了十年，据说从不大声就带得住人。俱乐部的会长坐在他旁边，双手平摊在旧台子的地面上。没人动。一个拿着文件夹的年轻人站在后面。主席一开口，满屋子的人都转向他。我们为预算争了一个钟头，然后他用一句话结束了会议。"},"child":{"tw":[["baby",3],["peanut",3],["offspring",2],["parent",1],["pregnant",6],["fry",0],["mother",6]],"en":"When my mother was pregnant with her second child, my father fried bread and eggs for us every morning. My baby sister slept in a small basket by the window, and I was told to be quiet. My parent would carry her on one arm while he did the rest. Someone gave us a bag of peanuts and we shared it. He said the offspring of a quiet house grow up calm. I did not understand it then, but I do now. We had very little, but nobody in that room felt poor.","zh":"我妈怀着第二个孩子的时候，我爸每天早上给我们煎面包和鸡蛋。我小妹睡在窗边的小篮子里，大人叫我别出声。我爹一只胳膊抱着她，另一只手把别的活干了。有人送了我们一袋花生，我们分着吃。他说安静人家养出的孩子性子也静。我那时不懂，现在懂了。我们没什么东西，可那间屋里谁都不觉得自己穷。"},"choice":{"tw":[["pick",0],["decision",3],["choose",6],["option",0],["pleasure",3],["neither",6],["prime",0]],"en":"I had a choice between two jobs in the same town. Neither option was perfect, and it was a hard decision. The first had better pay but long hours; the second was quiet and close to home. To pick between them was not easy. My father said the prime thing was not the money. You must choose for yourself, he told me. In the end I took the smaller office, and it was a pleasure to walk there each morning. Ten years later I still pass the other building and wonder, without regret.","zh":"同一个镇上有两份工作摆在我面前，我二选一。两个都不完美，这决定很难下。头一份钱多，可工时很长；第二份清静，离家也近。要在两者间挑一个并不容易。我父亲说，最要紧的不是钱。你得自己选，他对我说。最后我去了那间小办公室，每天走去上班都是件乐事。十年后我路过另一栋楼，还会想一想，但不后悔。"},"choose":{"tw":[["prefer",0],["field",3],["choice",6],["select",0],["elect",3],["want",6],["opt",0]],"en":"Every spring the village would choose a new leader for the field committee. People could select anyone they wanted, or they could opt to leave the paper blank. My uncle said he would prefer the older woman, though the choice was close. I wanted to elect someone young for a change. On the day of the vote, the whole square was quiet. He told me to choose carefully and not to follow the crowd. I marked my paper in the little booth and folded it twice. Walking home, I felt older than I was.","zh":"每年春天村里都要为农田委员会选一个新负责人。大家想选谁都行，也可以选择让那张纸空着。我叔说他更中意那位年长的女人，虽然两人票数很近。我倒想换换，选个年轻人上来。投票那天，整个广场很静。他叫我仔细选，别跟着人群走。我在小隔间里在纸上画了记号，折了两回。走回家时，我觉得自己比实际年龄老了些。"},"cold":{"tw":[["stale",0],["cool",5],["hot",1],["warm",6],["frigid",0],["chill",3],["dry",6]],"en":"The morning was cold and the air in the kitchen was dry. The bread from yesterday had gone stale, so my mother warmed it over the stove. She said a hot drink would help, but the water in the pot was only cool. I pulled my coat tight against the chill and stood by the window. Outside the wind was frigid and the ground was white. We did not talk much. She put a warm cup in my hands and told me to drink. That was the winter I learned that cold can be a kind of quiet.","zh":"那天早上很冷，厨房里的空气也干。昨天的面包已经不新鲜了，我妈在炉子上把它热了热。她说喝点热的好，可壶里的水只是温的。我紧了紧外套挡住那股寒气，站在窗边。外面风冷得刺骨，地上白茫茫的。我们没怎么说话。她把一只热杯子塞进我手里，让我喝。就是那个冬天，我知道了冷也可以是一种安静。"},"come":{"tw":[["arrive",2],["address",3],["change",2],["want",6],["fall",3],["land",3],["follow",0]],"en":"The letter did not come on Monday. It would arrive, my father said, but the post was slow after the storm. He had written the wrong address, and the change cost us a week. I wanted to follow it, so I walked to the office myself. Snow began to fall as I waited, and by the time I reached the door it had begun to land on my shoulders. The clerk found it at last, under a pile of papers. I read it standing up, and then I sat down on the step.","zh":"那封信星期一没来。我父亲说会到的，可风暴过后邮路慢。他把地址写错了，这一改耽误了我们一个星期。我想跟一跟，就自己走到了邮局。等的时候下起雪来，走到门口时，雪花已经落在我的肩上。职员终于找到了，压在一堆纸底下。我站着把信读完，然后在台阶上坐了下来。"},"dark":{"tw":[["black",5],["condition",2],["light",1],["bright",6],["blue",0],["pale",6],["night",3]],"en":"It was already dark when the light went out. The whole street turned black in a second, and only the pale moon showed. My sister's face looked blue in the cold. We sat on the floor and waited for the condition to improve, but the night was long. Then a small bright flame appeared in the window next door, and someone laughed. We laughed too. It was the first time in years that the street had been so quiet. Then the flame went to the next window, and the next, and the street came slowly back to life.","zh":"灯灭的时候天已经黑了。整条街一下子变成一片黑，只有淡淡的月亮亮着。我妹妹的脸在冷里显得发蓝。我们坐在地上，等情形好转，可那一夜很长。后来隔壁窗口亮起一小簇明亮的火苗，有人笑了一声。我们也笑了。那是多年来这条街头一回这么静。接着火苗移到下一个窗口，又一个窗口，街上慢慢又活了过来。"},"deep":{"tw":[["late",0],["middle",2],["shallow",1],["long",6],["thick",0],["apart",6],["bass",0]],"en":"The river was deep in the middle and shallow near the bank, so we had to walk apart to cast. It was late, and a thick fog hung over the water. My father said the bass would not bite in such cold. We stood a long way from the road and listened. Far off a drum sounded from the village. He told me to keep my line low and wait. It was the longest evening I remember. The fish never came. At dawn we folded the line and walked home, and he said nothing the whole way.","zh":"河中间很深，靠岸的地方浅，所以我们得分开站才能下钩。天已经晚了，水面上挂着厚雾。我父亲说这么冷鲈鱼不会咬钩。我们站在离大路很远的地方听动静。远处村里传来鼓声。他叫我压低钓线等着。那是我记得的最漫长的一个傍晚。鱼始终没来。天亮时我们收了线走回家，他一路上什么都没说。"},"doubt":{"tw":[["question",0],["misgiving",3],["distrust",2],["reason",6],["suspense",3],["disbelieve",2],["prove",6]],"en":"There was some doubt about who had taken the money. The clerk could not prove anything, and the manager began to distrust everyone in the room. I had a small misgiving of my own. The question was simple: who had the key that night? Nobody could answer, and the suspense was hard to bear. I did not disbelieve my friend, but I could not find a reason to defend him either. In the end the money was found in a coat, and nobody ever said sorry. I learned that doubt can sit in a room longer than any proof.","zh":"钱是谁拿的，这事有些说不清。职员什么都证明不了，经理开始不信任屋里的每一个人。我自己心里也有点不踏实。问题很简单：那晚钥匙在谁手里？谁都说不上来，那种悬着的滋味很难熬。我不是不信我朋友，可我也找不出什么理由替他说话。最后钱在一件外套里找到了，却没人道过歉。我明白了，疑心能在一间屋里待得比任何证据都久。"},"dry":{"tw":[["wry",0],["air",3],["change",2],["sweet",1],["water",6],["scorch",3],["cold",6]],"en":"The summer was dry and the air smelled of dust. Our small garden had begun to scorch in the sun, so we carried water from the well twice a day. My mother made a wry face when she saw the leaves. The change came at last with a cold wind from the hills. That evening the sky turned grey, and a sweet smell of rain filled the yard. We stood outside and let it fall on us. Nobody spoke for a long time. The garden did not recover that year, but the rain made us glad for a week.","zh":"那年夏天很干，空气里一股尘土味。我们的小园子开始被太阳烤焦，于是我们一天两趟从井里挑水。我妈看见叶子时撇了撇嘴。变化终于随一阵从山里来的冷风到了。傍晚天变灰，院子里满是雨要来的那种甜味。我们站在外面，任它淋在身上。很久谁都没说话。园子那年没能缓过来，可那场雨让我们高兴了一个星期。"}}});
